Gold Key: Voluntary intoxication may matter for a specific-intent element, but it is not a defense to a general-intent crime. General-intent battery requires intent to make the offensive contact, not a further objective.

Silver Key: When two “No” answers appear, do not pick the first one just because the outcome is right. Check whether the reason matches the stem’s offense classification.', NULL, 'REM-CRIM-INTOX-GENERAL-INTENT-01'),
  ('1094c8bc-d599-56e9-a829-c478b554b365', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17151_carol_program'), 'C', 'Yes, because intoxication negates any intent formed while drunk.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["drunk_means_no_intent","no_memory_means_no_intent","right_outcome_is_enough","battery_is_strict_liability"]', 'It converts the real intoxication idea into a global rule, which sounds intuitive when a person is drunk. The breaker is the Gold Key distinction: voluntary intoxication does not wipe out general intent.', 'The answer overclaims by saying intoxication negates any intent formed while drunk.', 'Mark ''any intent'' as an overclaim and classify the offense.', 'REM-CRIM-INTOX-GENERAL-INTENT-01'),
  ('060df5e9-bed8-5758-bcfa-b17768bf47a6', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17151_carol_program'), 'D', 'Yes, but only if Martha can show that she does not remember swinging the program.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["drunk_means_no_intent","no_memory_means_no_intent","right_outcome_is_enough","battery_is_strict_liability"]', 'It gives the student a concrete proof hook, no memory, which sounds like missing intent. The breaker is that later memory is not the same axis as intent at the moment, and the Gold Key still blocks voluntary intoxication for general-intent battery.', 'The answer invents a no-memory threshold and shifts away from intent at the moment of contact.', 'Ask what the call tests: defense availability, not recollection.', 'REM-CRIM-INTOX-GENERAL-INTENT-01'),
  ('73087cb5-f093-5742-9e71-67efe2f7c817', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17167_manger_lights_portal'), 'A', 'The portal may be valid if it is a proper means rationally related to carrying out the valid commerce regulation.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A is the only answer that is both valid-result and power-linked.', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-NP-01'),
  ('f3835348-df5d-58ef-b9a4-efbeeac714b0', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17167_manger_lights_portal'), 'B', 'The portal is invalid because federal tracking portals are never proper.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["necessary_means_indispensable","necessary_and_proper_is_freestanding","modern_database_suspicion"]', 'A student may distrust federal tracking systems and treat the answer as a principled limit on federal power. The breaker is the categorical word ''never,'' which overclaims the rule.', 'The answer overclaims by saying federal tracking portals are never proper.', 'Ask whether the answer bans an entire category without a trigger.', 'REM-CONLAW-NP-01'),
  ('c42fe21d-501d-53bb-b747-b495200b5472', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17167_manger_lights_portal'), 'C', 'The portal is invalid unless it is absolutely indispensable to the shipment rules.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["necessary_means_indispensable","necessary_and_proper_is_freestanding","modern_database_suspicion"]', 'A student may translate ''necessary'' into ordinary-language indispensability. The breaker is the Gold Key that Necessary and Proper does not require the only possible means.', 'The answer overclaims by requiring absolute indispensability.', 'Replace ''only possible'' with ''appropriate means connected to the power.''', 'REM-CONLAW-NP-01'),
  ('c83df7a6-e349-550b-94c2-d1e8165301f7', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17167_manger_lights_portal'), 'D', 'The portal is valid even if it has no connection to any enumerated power.', 0, '["flat_misstatement"]', '["necessary_means_indispensable","necessary_and_proper_is_freestanding","modern_database_suspicion"]', 'A student may see the word ''valid'' and stop reading before the reason. The breaker is that Necessary and Proper still needs an enumerated-power connection.', 'The answer removes the required enumerated-power connection.', 'Check whether the reason preserves the enumerated-power hook.', 'REM-CONLAW-NP-01'),
  ('b5db8ed0-2a16-5166-8f20-3607098d98e7', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17173_road_to_emmaus_puzzle_quest'), 'A', '$7,800, the difference between the reasonable value of the work and the agreed fee.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["reliance_equals_market_value","reasonable_value_overrides_bargain","no_recovery_if_reliance_unavailable","spread_is_damages"]', 'The student sees two dollar figures and tries to do bar-exam arithmetic. The breaker is that no rule in this call asks for the difference between value and price.', 'A invents a spread recovery from two stem numbers. The call asks for proper contract recovery, not a market-value-minus-price calculation.', 'Ask which number the contract itself makes legally operative.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-REMEDY-MENU-01'),
  ('37088b3c-9627-5ebd-994c-5fbe84317702', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17173_road_to_emmaus_puzzle_quest'), 'B', 'Nothing, because once Mary fully performed, reliance damages are unavailable.', 0, '["wrong_element","wrong_frame"]', '["reliance_equals_market_value","reasonable_value_overrides_bargain","no_recovery_if_reliance_unavailable","spread_is_damages"]', 'The student correctly senses that reliance is not the winning remedy label. The breaker is that the answer skips the contract-price recovery and therefore answers the wrong subquestion.', 'B reacts to the bad reliance label but skips the contract-price recovery that remains.', 'After rejecting reliance, identify the affirmative recovery still available.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-REMEDY-MENU-01'),
  ('b5a59791-3142-5d62-8716-19864f0a6be2', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17173_road_to_emmaus_puzzle_quest'), 'C', '$12,600, the agreed fee, because Mary fully performed and the expectation measure is readily fixed.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only C uses the fixed contract price and answers the proper-recovery call.', NULL, 'REM-CONTRACTS-REMEDY-MENU-01'),
  ('e3231009-87c5-5454-9579-b93a5c647122', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '17173_road_to_emmaus_puzzle_quest'), 'D', '$20,400, because reliance damages always use the reasonable value of services.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["reliance_equals_market_value","reasonable_value_overrides_bargain","no_recovery_if_reliance_unavailable","spread_is_damages"]', 'The student wants to award the higher value because Mary gave work worth more than the bargain. The breaker is the Gold Key: after full performance, fixed contract price controls over reasonable-value bait.', 'D overclaims with ''always'' and misuses reasonable value as a higher reliance measure.', 'Apply the bargain-price Gold Key when fixed price and full performance appear together.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-REMEDY-MENU-01'),
  ('917ed6f8-250d-5349-8e1c-f0979d5517d4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19177_manna_wagon_disposal'), 'A', 'invalid as a bill of attainder.', 0, '["wrong_element","wrong_frame"]', '["equal_protection_means_any_unfairness","bill_of_attainder_means_singling_out","Congress_has_general_police_power","valid_result_enough"]', 'A student sees Congress favoring one company and reaches for a severe constitutional label. The breaker is that bill-of-attainder analysis needs punishment, and the stem gives a sale.', 'The answer invokes a punishment doctrine, but the stem gives a sale/benefit and no punishment fact.', 'Ask: what was imposed on the alleged target, a burden or a benefit?', 'CONLAW-REMEDY-PROPERTY-SOURCE-01'),
  ('cd6c0344-8296-5f9b-b7ed-2251a16358f5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19177_manna_wagon_disposal'), 'B', 'valid under the Property Clause of Article IV.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. The challenged action is Congress selling property that belongs to the United States. Gold Key: when the stem gives federal property and Congress is disposing of it, lock the Property Clause as the power source before chasing fairness, punishment, or general police-power answers. Article IV, Section 3, Clause 2 gives Congress power to dispose of and regulate United States territory or other property, and official Constitution Annotated materials state that this clause covers “Territory or other Property belonging to the United States.” ([Congress.gov][1])

Silver Key: this is a four-doctrine-home array. Do not debate whether the sale is wise or fair. Match actor + object + action: Congress + federal property + sale.', NULL, 'CONLAW-REMEDY-PROPERTY-SOURCE-01'),
  ('1d7e64d9-fc29-5d08-957f-95acfe285748', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19177_manna_wagon_disposal'), 'C', 'invalid as a denial of equal protection under the Fourteenth Amendment.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["equal_protection_means_any_unfairness","bill_of_attainder_means_singling_out","Congress_has_general_police_power","valid_result_enough"]', 'A student sees unequal treatment between competitors and reaches for equal protection. The breaker is that this answer names the Fourteenth Amendment even though the actor is Congress.', 'The answer names a state-action source while the actor in the stem is Congress.', 'Ask: is the answer''s amendment aimed at this actor?', 'CONLAW-REMEDY-PROPERTY-SOURCE-01'),
  ('c56a522d-2706-5c8d-8535-5dc4d44d5b57', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19177_manna_wagon_disposal'), 'D', 'valid under the general police powers of Congress.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","wrong_frame"]', '["equal_protection_means_any_unfairness","bill_of_attainder_means_singling_out","Congress_has_general_police_power","valid_result_enough"]', 'A student likes the valid result and accepts the broad power label. The breaker is that Congress has no general police power, so the source must be a specific enumerated power.', 'The answer gives the right result but relies on a nonexistent general federal police power.', 'Replace generic power labels with the specific enumerated power that matches the facts.', 'CONLAW-REMEDY-PROPERTY-SOURCE-01'),
  ('fab35e35-a9fe-5212-a7d6-103f4ed7db10', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19194_loaves_pages'), 'A', 'The statute is subject to strict scrutiny because it discriminates against gay and lesbian persons on the basis of sexual orientation, which is a suspect classification.', 0, '["flat_misstatement"]', '["tradition_is_always_legitimate","sympathetic_class_means_strict_scrutiny","no_benefit_right_ends_equal_protection","federal_benefits_power_is_plenary"]', 'Strict scrutiny feels like the strongest answer for a law affecting same-sex couples. The breaker is that Windsor did not expressly make sexual orientation a suspect classification.', 'The choice overpromotes Windsor into strict scrutiny based on suspect-class status.', 'Ask whether the controlling case actually declared suspect-class status.', 'REM-CONLAW-WINDSOR-BARE-ANIMUS'),
  ('439c1cc8-9272-53c5-8dff-5e861a9c3759', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19194_loaves_pages'), 'B', 'The statute survives rational basis review because Congress has a legitimate interest in using one uniform definition of marriage across federal programs and preserving the traditional definition of marriage.', 0, '["flat_misstatement"]', '["tradition_is_always_legitimate","sympathetic_class_means_strict_scrutiny","no_benefit_right_ends_equal_protection","federal_benefits_power_is_plenary"]', 'Rational basis plus tradition and uniformity sounds like ordinary Con Law deference. The breaker is the Windsor/Romer Gold Key that bare animus or dignity injury is not legitimate.', 'The choice treats uniformity and tradition as sufficient rational-basis interests even under Windsor/Romer bare-animus facts.', 'Check whether the stated interests mask a purpose/effect to demean an identifiable group.', 'REM-CONLAW-WINDSOR-BARE-ANIMUS'),
  ('666d9405-f120-50e0-bd23-4eaa80bf0233', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19194_loaves_pages'), 'C', 'The statute survives because Congress controls federal benefit programs, and there is no constitutional right to receive a spousal federal benefit.', 0, '["misfit","wrong_frame"]', '["tradition_is_always_legitimate","sympathetic_class_means_strict_scrutiny","no_benefit_right_ends_equal_protection","federal_benefits_power_is_plenary"]', 'Congress’s control over federal benefit programs sounds like a powerful threshold answer. The breaker is that the call asks Equal Protection classification, not entitlement to the benefit.', 'The choice answers benefits authority and entitlement, not the Equal Protection classification question.', 'Restate the call as Equal Protection classification and ask why the line was drawn.', 'REM-CONLAW-WINDSOR-BARE-ANIMUS'),
  ('8fd32eaa-73e8-51ec-9b1a-4bcb2093c188', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19194_loaves_pages'), 'D', 'The statute fails Equal Protection review because denying federal recognition to lawfully married same-sex couples serves only to demean their status, and a bare desire to harm an identifiable group is not a legitimate governmental interest under any level of scrutiny.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'D is the best answer. Gold Key: A federal marriage-recognition law that denies federal benefits to same-sex spouses who are lawfully married under state law fails when its purpose and effect are to impose a separate, lesser status on those marriages. Silver Key: Do not let “Congress controls benefits” or “no one has a right to a benefit” answer the wrong question. The call is Equal Protection: why did the government draw this line?

The statute denies federal recognition to a marriage the state has made lawful. The answer does not need to promote sexual orientation to suspect-class status. It also does not ask whether federal benefits exist as a free-standing right. It asks whether this classification may be justified. Under the controlling Windsor/Romer line, a bare desire to demean or injure an identifiable group is not a legitimate governmental interest.', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-WINDSOR-BARE-ANIMUS'),
  ('118eb807-2f81-5f22-ba41-0d84fb70a34d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19213_road_to_emmaus_breezeway'), 'A', 'Lydia owed a duty because Esther had just finished a paid puzzle session.', 0, '["wrong_element","wrong_frame"]', '["business_as_insurer","customer_status_auto_duty","inherent_danger_label"]', 'It notices that Esther was a paying participant, so it feels like the premises relationship is solved. The breaker is that the call asks for a guard-duty trigger, and paid status alone does not make a random attack foreseeable.', 'Uses a real status fact but does not answer the security-guard duty trigger.', 'Ask: what fact made guards necessary before the attack?', 'RC-TORTS-SECURITY-DUTY-01'),
  ('69b75bbb-b778-5fc2-8746-979c88c4aff7', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19213_road_to_emmaus_breezeway'), 'B', 'Lydia owed a duty because every business must prevent all crimes on its premises.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["business_as_insurer","customer_status_auto_duty","inherent_danger_label"]', 'It converts the broad idea of business safety into a simple protective rule. The breaker is the absolute wording: every business and all crimes turns premises liability into insurance.', 'Every business/all crimes is an absolute insurance duty.', 'Circle every/all and test whether the law is really absolute.', 'RC-TORTS-SECURITY-DUTY-01'),
  ('eaf8a165-a10b-5634-ac5b-d136bdb26fbb', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19213_road_to_emmaus_breezeway'), 'C', 'Lydia likely had no duty to post security guards because the random attack was not made foreseeable by prior similar incidents, a created danger, or another guard-duty trigger.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is the best answer.

Silver Key: Lock the exact duty. The question is not “was Esther a paying customer?” It is “did these facts trigger a duty to post security guards against a random third-party attack?”

Gold Key: A business is not an insurer against random third-party crime. Customer status matters, but a guard/security duty needs a foreseeability trigger: prior similar incidents, created risk, imminent danger, or comparable notice.

The stem gives six quiet years, an unknown stranger, and no created danger. That makes C the only answer tied to the duty the lawsuit actually claims.', NULL, 'RC-TORTS-SECURITY-DUTY-01'),
  ('e6c70ae8-3a23-52da-82e3-cb21a6f0dd1a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19213_road_to_emmaus_breezeway'), 'D', 'Lydia owed a duty because exit breezeways are inherently dangerous as a matter of law.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["business_as_insurer","customer_status_auto_duty","inherent_danger_label"]', 'It sounds lawyerly because it declares a category dangerous as a matter of law. The breaker is that no stem fact supports automatic danger for every exit breezeway.', 'Invents an inherent-danger category for exit breezeways.', 'Ask whether the answer names a real trigger or merely labels a location dangerous.', 'RC-TORTS-SECURITY-DUTY-01'),
  ('dd395933-0607-5873-bde0-7854ffbbe32d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19228_prayer_card_study_bible'), 'A', 'Sustain the objection only if Ruth refuses to testify.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["marital_privilege_is_only_spoken","documents_cannot_be_communications","witness_spouse_controls_all_spousal_privileges"]', 'The student remembers that a spouse may have a refusal-to-testify privilege and imports that neighbor rule. The breaker is that Daniel asserts the communication privilege over the message itself.', 'This answers the witness-spouse refusal frame rather than Daniel’s communication-privilege objection.', 'Separate communications privilege from testimonial refusal.', 'EVI-PRIV-OBJECT-NOT-MEDIUM-01'),
  ('74d9ed64-dedb-5265-bd98-cb1ccb7110cd', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19228_prayer_card_study_bible'), 'B', 'Overrule the objection, because the prayer-card is a document rather than a communication.', 0, '["flat_misstatement"]', '["marital_privilege_is_only_spoken","documents_cannot_be_communications","witness_spouse_controls_all_spousal_privileges"]', 'The student sees a physical prayer-card and treats the card’s format as the legal object. The breaker is that a document can embody the protected confidential communication.', 'This treats document status as defeating communication status.', 'Name the protected object before naming the medium.', 'EVI-PRIV-OBJECT-NOT-MEDIUM-01'),
  ('7321d2d7-0dcb-5b83-bafe-388d12635e6d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19228_prayer_card_study_bible'), 'C', 'Sustain the objection, because a confidential written message between spouses during marriage can be a protected marital communication.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. The prayer-card is written, but that does not defeat the privilege. Gold Key: marital communications privilege protects the confidential spouse-to-spouse communication made during marriage; the protected object is the confidential communication, not the medium. Silver Key: when the answers fight over “spoken words,” “document,” and “refuses to testify,” sort the array by object: communication object beats evidence format and witness-choice bait.', NULL, 'EVI-PRIV-OBJECT-NOT-MEDIUM-01'),
  ('1b60a283-6117-5767-9a08-0a3716850d25', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19228_prayer_card_study_bible'), 'D', 'Overrule the objection, because the privilege protects only spoken words.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["marital_privilege_is_only_spoken","documents_cannot_be_communications","witness_spouse_controls_all_spousal_privileges"]', 'The student equates marital communications with spoken conversation. The breaker is the invented oral-only limit.', 'This invents an oral-only limitation.', 'Treat ''only spoken words'' as an invented restriction.', 'EVI-PRIV-OBJECT-NOT-MEDIUM-01'),
  ('471e1fd9-a568-59f4-a798-18f0a102a6da', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19250_scripture_card_printer'), 'A', 'Stephen can recover only in restitution because the express condition failed.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["satisfaction_means_total_discretion","honest_dislike_defeats_payment","condition_failure_triggers_restitution"]', 'It sounds precise because it gives Stephen a fallback remedy after a supposed failed condition. The breaker is that the performance metric was met under the commercial-utility Gold Key, so the condition did not fail.', 'The choice assumes the express condition failed; under the commercial-output standard, the output metric was met.', 'Apply the Gold Key, then compare 3,200 required to 3,360 actual.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-SATISFACTION-OBJECT-01'),
  ('bc14b1f5-d121-566a-8da1-ae959c85136e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19250_scripture_card_printer'), 'B', 'Lydia''s satisfaction is judged by an objective commercial standard, and the rent condition is satisfied if the printer met the required commercial performance.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. The clause asks whether Lydia is satisfied that the printer produces a stated commercial output. That is a measurable performance target, not a personal-aesthetic taste term. Gold Key: a satisfaction clause about commercial utility or mechanical performance is judged objectively when a reasonable-person test is practicable. Silver Key: underline what the party must be satisfied *about* before honoring “I was not satisfied.” Here, the target is 3,200 finished cards per hour, and the printer produced 3,360. The rent condition is satisfied.', NULL, 'REM-CONTRACTS-SATISFACTION-OBJECT-01'),
  ('9639f541-c6c1-5f89-84ac-3ad113a5baae', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19250_scripture_card_printer'), 'C', 'Lydia may refuse rent because any satisfaction clause gives unlimited subjective discretion.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["satisfaction_means_total_discretion","honest_dislike_defeats_payment","condition_failure_triggers_restitution"]', 'It sells the broad student myth that satisfaction words always make the buyer the judge. The breaker is the absolute any/unlimited language, which collapses a measured-performance clause into personal whim.', 'The words any and unlimited make the choice structurally overbroad.', 'Mark any/unlimited as the tell.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-SATISFACTION-OBJECT-01'),
  ('3cd9e608-2cb4-5a34-81fc-18a313191ebe', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19250_scripture_card_printer'), 'D', 'Lydia may refuse rent if she honestly dislikes any aspect of the printer.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["satisfaction_means_total_discretion","honest_dislike_defeats_payment","condition_failure_triggers_restitution"]', 'It sells a familiar honesty idea: if Lydia truly dislikes the printer, satisfaction sounds absent. The breaker is the wrong frame; this clause asks about output, not personal taste.', 'The choice answers a personal-taste satisfaction question, not the measurable-output condition in the stem.', 'Ask: satisfied about what?', 'REM-CONTRACTS-SATISFACTION-OBJECT-01'),
  ('25b50c35-233b-557b-8153-5f23c717d87c', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19263_chapel_handbells'), 'A', 'Embezzlement, because Lydia was entrusted with the handbells in a private sale for a Christian music program.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["fraud_equals_larceny_by_trick","transaction_equals_entrustment","bad_check_equals_false_pretense_basis","ignores_title_transfer"]', 'It sees a transaction and turns that into an entrustment story. The breaker is that Paul transferred ownership because of Lydia''s lie, not lawful custody for later conversion.', 'Embezzlement is the neighboring lawful-custody frame; the stem gives ownership transfer by deception.', 'Ask whether Lydia first had lawful custody or whether ownership moved because of fraud.', 'CRIM-02'),
  ('f126b8d2-0ce2-5cef-a012-557bfbd1bcc9', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19263_chapel_handbells'), 'B', 'False pretenses, because Lydia obtained ownership of the handbell sets by a knowingly false representation of a present fact.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B alone matches the transfer mechanic and the operative false statement.', NULL, 'CRIM-02'),
  ('6a8dbfc6-0605-519b-a858-8bd717777308', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19263_chapel_handbells'), 'C', 'Larceny by trick, because Lydia used fraudulent misrepresentations to obtain the handbells.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["fraud_equals_larceny_by_trick","transaction_equals_entrustment","bad_check_equals_false_pretense_basis","ignores_title_transfer"]', 'It sees deception and reaches for the familiar deception crime. The breaker is the bill of sale transferring ownership, which moves the case off the possession-only lane.', 'Larceny by trick is the neighboring possession-only frame; the bill of sale makes ownership the split.', 'Find whether Paul transferred ownership or only possession.', 'CRIM-02'),
  ('e2b6fb83-5a1d-53e1-8837-587b080c8e99', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19263_chapel_handbells'), 'D', 'False pretenses, because Lydia''s check was drawn on a closed account, constituting a false promise of future payment.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["fraud_equals_larceny_by_trick","transaction_equals_entrustment","bad_check_equals_false_pretense_basis","ignores_title_transfer"]', 'It notices the closed-account check and treats that as the false-pretense basis. The breaker is that the check is intent evidence while the operative present-fact lie is Lydia''s claimed role.', 'The bad check supports intent but does not supply the operative present-fact representation.', 'Separate intent evidence from the present-fact lie that caused the transfer.', 'CRIM-02'),
  ('ce60514a-3d5c-566e-9e80-fbee1e4f0bf9', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19266_carol_banquet_jmol'), 'A', 'Grant JMOL only if Lydia proves Daniel filed the complaint in bad faith.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","procedural_frame"]', '["jury_must_always_decide","bad_faith_controls_jmol","sympathy_can_replace_evidence"]', 'The choice borrows a seriousness screen from filing or sanctions language, so it sounds like a gatekeeping standard. The breaker is that the motion targets trial evidence on one element, not the plaintiff''s motive for filing.', 'The choice invents a bad-faith filing threshold for a motion that targets evidentiary sufficiency at trial.', 'Ask whether the motion attacks filing conduct or trial evidence on the target element.', 'CIV-REM-JMOL-EVIDENCE-GATE-01'),
  ('b5aecb93-be0b-502c-ad2b-bf62f6ff4884', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19266_carol_banquet_jmol'), 'B', 'Deny JMOL automatically because any civil case that reaches trial must go to the jury.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","procedural_frame"]', '["jury_must_always_decide","bad_faith_controls_jmol","sympathy_can_replace_evidence"]', 'The choice flatters the jury-trial instinct that once evidence starts, everything belongs to the jury. The breaker is the absolute word automatically, because Rule 50 is the trial tool for legally insufficient evidence.', 'The choice overclaims that any civil case reaching trial must automatically go to the jury.', 'Mark automatically and any civil case, then recall that Rule 50 is the evidence gate.', 'CIV-REM-JMOL-EVIDENCE-GATE-01'),
  ('308a6a32-514b-58d8-8d50-6bb9370cc5c0', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19266_carol_banquet_jmol'), 'C', 'Grant JMOL if no reasonable jury would have a legally sufficient evidentiary basis to find for Daniel on the agreement element.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only C is true and responsive under the Rule 50 anchor and the stem’s no-evidence trigger.', NULL, 'CIV-REM-JMOL-EVIDENCE-GATE-01'),
  ('6af159fb-e1ce-5136-9a90-49bce15266a7', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19266_carol_banquet_jmol'), 'D', 'Deny JMOL if the judge personally thinks Daniel’s carol banquet is sympathetic.', 0, '["colloquialism"]', '["jury_must_always_decide","bad_faith_controls_jmol","sympathy_can_replace_evidence"]', 'The choice turns a sympathetic Christian event into a reason to keep the case alive. The breaker is that sympathy is not evidence on the targeted element.', 'The choice substitutes sympathy for evidence on the targeted element.', 'Ask whether the reason supplies evidence a jury could use.', 'CIV-REM-JMOL-EVIDENCE-GATE-01'),
  ('b3163155-23bf-5446-9dce-2ecbeac63d65', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19286_five_loaves_press'), 'A', 'The court must instruct the jury that the missing project-board notes were unfavorable to Five Loaves Press.', 0, '["backwards","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["lost_evidence_equals_bad_fact","spoliation_equals_default","informal_esi_not_discoverable","prejudice_equals_intent"]', 'A student sees lost notes and wants the jury to assume the worst. The breaker is the missing intent gate for unfavorable-inference sanctions.', 'This applies an intent-based jury-inference sanction when the stem gives prejudice but no intent.', 'Ask: prejudice-only track or intent-based track?', 'REM-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-LOST-ESI-01'),
  ('5e393fbb-68ce-54ad-b9ca-de723a836ca0', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19286_five_loaves_press'), 'B', 'The court may do nothing because electronically stored project-board notes are not discoverable.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["lost_evidence_equals_bad_fact","spoliation_equals_default","informal_esi_not_discoverable","prejudice_equals_intent"]', 'A student may treat electronic project-board notes as informal and outside discovery. The breaker is that the answer invents a categorical ESI exclusion.', 'This fabricates a categorical rule that electronic project-board notes are not discoverable.', 'Treat broad ''not discoverable'' statements as suspect unless a named rule supports them.', 'REM-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-LOST-ESI-01'),
  ('6a560d94-d949-5311-90e8-1ee3065a63f8', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19286_five_loaves_press'), 'C', 'The court may order measures no greater than necessary to cure the prejudice caused by the missing notes.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is the only answer calibrated to prejudice without intent.', NULL, 'REM-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-LOST-ESI-01'),
  ('8b2e4667-81c6-5f3c-9013-d12dd164b55f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19286_five_loaves_press'), 'D', 'The court must enter a case-ending sanction whenever any electronically stored information is lost.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["lost_evidence_equals_bad_fact","spoliation_equals_default","informal_esi_not_discoverable","prejudice_equals_intent"]', 'A student may think spoliation always deserves the harshest punishment. The breaker is the automatic wording: must, whenever any.', 'This makes a case-ending sanction automatic whenever any ESI is lost.', 'Replace automatic punishment with calibrated sanction ladder.', 'REM-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-LOST-ESI-01'),
  ('895134ff-f6d1-5e7d-8831-52421f6770fa', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19336_nativity_warehouse_rescue'), 'A', 'Yes, but only if Timothy asked Ruth to intervene.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["alter_ego_majority_confusion","request_required_myth","must_witness_start_myth","hidden_truth_overweights_reasonable_belief"]', 'It sells the cognitive move that a bystander should wait for permission before using force. The breaker is that majority defense of others requires reasonable necessity, not a request.', 'Adds a request requirement not present in the majority defense-of-others rule.', 'Ask whether the rule says request, relationship, or reasonable necessity.', 'CRIM-ANCHOR-DEFENSE-OTHERS-01'),
  ('27f4edc2-fad1-50ab-96af-d999d2afef0a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19336_nativity_warehouse_rescue'), 'B', 'Yes, because Ruth reasonably believed Timothy was being unlawfully attacked and that using force was necessary.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is the only answer that is both true under the Gold Key and responsive to the majority-rule call.', NULL, 'CRIM-ANCHOR-DEFENSE-OTHERS-01'),
  ('0a843240-3135-5358-b757-8b47b92b1d57', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19336_nativity_warehouse_rescue'), 'C', 'No, because Daniel actually had the right to use force, making Ruth’s intervention unjustified.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["alter_ego_majority_confusion","request_required_myth","must_witness_start_myth","hidden_truth_overweights_reasonable_belief"]', 'It sells the hidden-truth move: Daniel really was justified, so Ruth should lose. The breaker is that the call selects the majority reasonable-appearance rule, not the alter-ego rule.', 'Uses the alter-ego actual-rights frame instead of the majority reasonable-appearance frame.', 'Name the axis: majority reasonable appearance versus actual-rights alter ego.', 'CRIM-ANCHOR-DEFENSE-OTHERS-01'),
  ('b5c28a10-e042-5a2d-b505-c1a438c6fcb1', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19336_nativity_warehouse_rescue'), 'D', 'No, because Ruth did not personally witness Timothy’s earlier attack on Daniel.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["alter_ego_majority_confusion","request_required_myth","must_witness_start_myth","hidden_truth_overweights_reasonable_belief"]', 'It sells the idea that Ruth needed the whole history before acting. The breaker is that the majority rule allows action on a reasonable belief from the circumstances she saw.', 'Adds an eyewitness-origin requirement not present in the majority defense-of-others rule.', 'Ask whether the answer adds a condition not in the Gold Key.', 'CRIM-ANCHOR-DEFENSE-OTHERS-01'),
  ('525dd7e4-2003-5e3e-bcc0-1b584762e957', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19379_hymn_candle_invoice_van'), 'A', 'Overrule the objection because incriminating statements between spouses are never privileged in a criminal case.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["divorce_ends_all_spousal_privilege","criminal_confessions_never_privileged","correct_result_wrong_route"]', 'A student may think incriminating criminal statements should always come in. The breaker is that incriminating content alone does not erase a valid confidential marital communication privilege.', 'The word never overclaims; incriminating content does not itself erase communications privilege.', 'Ask whether any privilege route survives despite incriminating content.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-SPOUSAL-19379-01'),
  ('3b9c24b6-3d80-5bac-b2a5-25deda3c65fe', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19379_hymn_candle_invoice_van'), 'B', 'Sustain the objection if Timothy’s statement was a confidential marital communication made during the marriage; divorce ends the adverse spousal testimonial privilege, but it does not by itself eliminate the marital communications privilege for prior confidential communications.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. Gold Key: spousal testimonial privilege and confidential marital communications privilege are separate routes. The testimonial privilege depends on a current marriage; the communications privilege can protect confidential private communications made during the marriage even after divorce.

Silver Key: when the array splits “sustain/overrule” and “testimonial/communications,” match the privilege route to the timing facts. Timothy and Lydia are divorced now, but the statement was private and made while they were married. The communications route, not the testimonial route, is the responsive route.', NULL, 'REM-EVIDENCE-SPOUSAL-19379-01'),
  ('eff34b14-0efa-5135-b989-f5a747939925', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19379_hymn_candle_invoice_van'), 'C', 'Overrule the objection because divorce ends every spousal privilege for statements made during the marriage.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["divorce_ends_all_spousal_privilege","criminal_confessions_never_privileged","correct_result_wrong_route"]', 'A student may know divorce matters and overapply that fact to every spousal privilege. The breaker is the Gold Key distinction between testimonial privilege and confidential communications privilege.', 'The word every collapses two spousal privileges into one divorce rule.', 'Separate testimonial privilege from confidential marital communications privilege.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-SPOUSAL-19379-01'),
  ('f3302a61-da43-5be8-9846-093187d3b944', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19379_hymn_candle_invoice_van'), 'D', 'Sustain the objection under the adverse spousal testimonial privilege because Lydia is being asked to testify adversely against Timothy.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["divorce_ends_all_spousal_privilege","criminal_confessions_never_privileged","correct_result_wrong_route"]', 'A student may stop at the correct surface result, sustain. The breaker is that the route is adverse testimonial privilege, and the divorce fact points away from that route.', 'It reaches sustain under the wrong privilege route.', 'Between two sustain answers, choose the privilege route that matches the timing facts.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-SPOUSAL-19379-01'),
  ('c3a97a30-2a04-50ff-8676-74bec0253126', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19381_shepherd_olive_press_deed'), 'A', 'Naomi, because a deed that is not recorded is void.', 0, '["flat_misstatement"]', '["unrecorded means void","recorder stamp required","title passes only upon recording"]', 'This sells the harsh memory that missing a public filing kills a property transfer. The breaker is the Gold Key: recording protects priority, not validity between the original parties.', 'This choice states the recording myth in its harshest form: unrecorded equals void.', 'Apply the Gold Key and ask whether a protected third party appears.', 'RP-ANCHOR-RECORDING-VALIDITY-01'),
  ('fc2f686d-d147-588a-b74f-cd348bceec31', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19381_shepherd_olive_press_deed'), 'B', 'Naomi, because the county recorder’s stamp is a deed-validity formality.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["unrecorded means void","recorder stamp required","title passes only upon recording"]', 'This sells a formalities reflex by turning the recorder’s stamp into another deed requirement. The breaker is that the stem already gives the deed-validity facts and the stamp belongs to recording.', 'This choice invents a recorder-stamp deed-validity requirement.', 'Use the stem: all required deed terms were already supplied.', 'RP-ANCHOR-RECORDING-VALIDITY-01'),
  ('563ff726-0427-59a6-8661-2fa93653dd0b', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19381_shepherd_olive_press_deed'), 'C', 'Lydia, because recording is not required for a valid deed to pass title between grantor and grantee.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. The stem gives the title-transfer facts: Naomi signed the deed, delivered it, Lydia accepted it, and the deed contained the required deed terms. No outsider claims the parcel. That makes the question a validity-between-the-parties question, not a recording-priority question.

Gold Key: A valid deed passes title between grantor and grantee when delivered and accepted; recording protects notice and priority against outsiders, not validity between the original parties.

Silver Key: Read the answer array as a 3-vs-1 recording trap. Three choices give the property back to Naomi because of recording; one choice answers the actual call: title between the original parties.', NULL, 'RP-ANCHOR-RECORDING-VALIDITY-01'),
  ('e10117cc-eae1-5e9b-9aa8-2e7c0b9c2627', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19381_shepherd_olive_press_deed'), 'D', 'Naomi, until Lydia records the deed.', 0, '["backwards"]', '["unrecorded means void","recorder stamp required","title passes only upon recording"]', 'This sells a timing compromise: Lydia will own later, after recording. The breaker is that title passed when the valid deed was delivered and accepted; no later recording step is needed between these parties.', 'This choice reverses the timing by treating recording as the event that passes title.', 'Delivery and acceptance do the title-passing work; recording is not the timing gate here.', 'RP-ANCHOR-RECORDING-VALIDITY-01'),
  ('a8a885b5-8a96-5b46-aa06-2c14b15b04f5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19386_scripture_audio_cap'), 'A', 'Hannah may enforce the promise only up to the contract''s $12,000 liability cap.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is true and responsive after C is cut for overclaim, B for wrong route, and D under the same-contract cap axis.', NULL, 'REM-CONTRACTS-TPB-PACKAGE-01'),
  ('b0822cfd-c3c4-599f-a091-f022c4410dc8', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19386_scripture_audio_cap'), 'B', 'Hannah may recover only if Peter first assigns her the audio-service contract.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["nonparty_not_bound_by_limit","privity_blocks_all_beneficiaries","assignment_required_for_tpb","cap_does_not_travel"]', 'Assignment sounds like a legitimate way for a nonparty to receive contract rights. The breaker is that the stem already supplies third-party-beneficiary status, so assignment answers the wrong route.', 'Assignment is a real contract-rights route, but it answers a different route from the one in the stem.', 'Say: ''TPB route is already in the stem; assignment is not required.''', 'REM-CONTRACTS-TPB-PACKAGE-01'),
  ('976e7b07-1a8e-527c-b920-b2a7278da610', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19386_scripture_audio_cap'), 'C', 'Hannah cannot recover anything because beneficiaries can never enforce audio-service contracts.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["nonparty_not_bound_by_limit","privity_blocks_all_beneficiaries","assignment_required_for_tpb","cap_does_not_travel"]', 'The privity reflex makes it feel safe to say an outsider gets nothing. The breaker is the categorical word ''never,'' because intended beneficiaries are not categorically barred from enforcing service contracts.', 'The word ''never'' overstates the rule by denying all intended-beneficiary enforcement of audio-service contracts.', 'Circle ''never'' and ask whether the stem directly names the beneficiary.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-TPB-PACKAGE-01'),
  ('bf0a2822-cc5e-556c-a767-54832d0c30c9', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19386_scripture_audio_cap'), 'D', 'Hannah may recover the full $26,000 because she did not sign the liability cap.', 0, '["backwards","wrong_frame"]', '["nonparty_not_bound_by_limit","privity_blocks_all_beneficiaries","assignment_required_for_tpb","cap_does_not_travel"]', 'Nonparty status makes the liability cap feel like a private bargain Hannah never accepted. The breaker is the package rule: Hannah''s enforcement right and the cap come from the same contract.', 'The answer reverses the package rule by letting Hannah use the contract for the right while escaping the same contract''s cap.', 'Ask: ''What document creates the right, and what document creates the limit?''', 'REM-CONTRACTS-TPB-PACKAGE-01'),
  ('30653799-5f24-5ade-8036-fd5207a966ff', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19430_harp_instructor_olive_grove'), 'A', 'Daniel, because the role description identified a specific person when the deed was delivered.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A is correct. The deed uses a role description, not Daniel’s personal name. Gold Key: A deed can identify a grantee by an office or role if one person fitting that description is reasonably ascertainable when the deed is delivered. Silver Key: Read the recipient phrase before reading the formalities traps: “to the harp instructor” points first to the person who holds that role, not automatically to the school and not back to the grantor.

Daniel was the only harp instructor at the moment of delivery, and he accepted the deed. That makes Daniel the ascertainable grantee.', NULL, 'RP-DEED-ROLE-GRANTEE-01'),
  ('e63cc0af-03ad-5cc4-872b-df4b6ebc05b7', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19430_harp_instructor_olive_grove'), 'B', 'Lydia, because Daniel did not sign the deed.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["personal_name_required","grantee_signature_required","organization_named_inside_phrase_owns","contract_formality_import"]', 'The student imports the contract habit that the recipient must sign. The breaker is the deed Gold Key: the grantee accepts, but generally need not sign.', 'Adds a required grantee signature that the Gold Key rejects.', 'Separate grantor execution from grantee acceptance.', 'RP-DEED-ROLE-GRANTEE-01'),
  ('d6a5f648-0cb0-549c-a079-06da28fbf2ef', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19430_harp_instructor_olive_grove'), 'C', 'Lydia, because a deed must state the grantee’s personal name.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["personal_name_required","grantee_signature_required","organization_named_inside_phrase_owns","contract_formality_import"]', 'The student over-formalizes the deed and thinks only a personal name can work. The breaker is the ascertainability Gold Key: the role description can identify Daniel.', 'Adds a personal-name requirement that the Gold Key rejects.', 'Ask whether exactly one person fit the role at delivery.', 'RP-DEED-ROLE-GRANTEE-01'),
  ('bacb807e-86f1-50ef-b4e2-bc864a7f227a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19430_harp_instructor_olive_grove'), 'D', 'Capernaum Hymn School, because the role title automatically makes the school the grantee.', 0, '["flat_misstatement"]', '["personal_name_required","grantee_signature_required","organization_named_inside_phrase_owns","contract_formality_import"]', 'The student sees Capernaum Hymn School inside the phrase and jumps to the organization. The breaker is the recipient phrase: the deed says to the harp instructor, not to the school.', 'Changes the recipient from the role-holder to the school.', 'Read “to the harp instructor” as pointing to the role-holder.', 'RP-DEED-ROLE-GRANTEE-01'),
  ('6452f404-d83d-5fea-8c8e-c661fedd8a39', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19434_hymn_hands_stimulator'), 'A', 'Yes, because Lydia was injured by the exact risk described in the warning.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["patient_must_always_be_warned_directly","injury_equals_defect","prescription_products_are_immune"]', 'The student sees that the harm matched the warning and treats injury as the missing puzzle piece. The breaker is that injury proves damage, while the call asks whether the warning duty was breached.', 'This choice proves injury by the warned-of risk, not failure to warn.', 'Name the missing element: warning defect or warning audience.', 'REM-TORTS-LI-01'),
  ('6271585b-5e69-5a2f-bca0-26d30c4bab79', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19434_hymn_hands_stimulator'), 'B', 'No, because prescription medical devices are exempt from all products liability claims.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["patient_must_always_be_warned_directly","injury_equals_defect","prescription_products_are_immune"]', 'The student overcorrects for the special status of prescription products and converts a special warning rule into total immunity. The breaker is the word all, which overstates the result and dodges the actual warning-duty reason.', 'This choice overclaims by saying prescription medical devices are exempt from all products liability claims.', 'Mark the word all and ask whether the result is narrower.', 'REM-TORTS-LI-01'),
  ('8e33977a-0c24-57c0-9c0a-4f7705057c7d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19434_hymn_hands_stimulator'), 'C', 'Yes, because makers of prescription medical devices must always warn patients directly.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["patient_must_always_be_warned_directly","injury_equals_defect","prescription_products_are_immune"]', 'The student hears patient safety and assumes direct warning is always required. The breaker is the Gold Key: in this jurisdiction the prescribing physician can be the warning audience.', 'This choice overclaims by saying direct patient warning is always required despite the learned-intermediary rule.', 'Apply the learned-intermediary distinction.', 'REM-TORTS-LI-01'),
  ('b5a468d7-a46c-5f48-b206-cbe81f2969b5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19434_hymn_hands_stimulator'), 'D', 'No, because Barnabas Biotech adequately warned Stephen, the prescribing physician, who served as the learned intermediary.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'After A, B, and C each break one filter, D is the only true-and-responsive answer.', NULL, 'REM-TORTS-LI-01'),
  ('107ce665-631b-576f-a1fc-12ccd2995efd', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19448_praise_night_tshirt_cannon'), 'A', 'Yes, because negligent entrustment makes Lydia strictly liable for any injury caused by the T-shirt cannon.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["title_equals_control","injury_equals_strict_liability","operator_alone_breaks_duty"]', 'The injury makes automatic liability feel satisfying because the chattel was dangerous. The breaker is that ''strictly liable'' and ''any injury'' overstate a negligence theory.', 'The answer converts a negligence-duty theory into strict liability for any injury.', 'Circle ''strictly'' and ''any'' and cut the overclaim.', 'RC-TORTS-NE-001'),
  ('2e4992d7-ef5e-536a-9c5e-3fff81cf5844', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19448_praise_night_tshirt_cannon'), 'B', 'No, because only the legal owner of a chattel can be liable for negligent entrustment.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["title_equals_control","injury_equals_strict_liability","operator_alone_breaks_duty"]', 'Formal title sounds like the clean legal gate for responsibility over property. The breaker is the Gold Key: negligent entrustment looks to control or supply, not just ownership.', 'The answer invents a legal-owner-only gate that the Gold Key defeats.', 'Ask whether the defendant supplied or controlled access to the chattel.', 'RC-TORTS-NE-001'),
  ('24ef69ba-c605-5135-ae2e-00e9a2a88ac0', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19448_praise_night_tshirt_cannon'), 'C', 'No, because Barnabas alone fired the cannon and third-party conduct always cuts off Lydia''s duty.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["title_equals_control","injury_equals_strict_liability","operator_alone_breaks_duty"]', 'Barnabas physically fired the cannon, so the student may stop at the operator. The breaker is the word ''always'' and the call-focus move: Lydia''s duty can arise from foreseeable misuse by the person she supplied.', 'The answer overclaims that third-party conduct always cuts off the target defendant''s duty.', 'Reject ''always'' and ask whether the third-party misuse was the foreseeable risk.', 'RC-TORTS-NE-001'),
  ('6ced83c3-86a7-571b-90b2-a7917b5dfde8', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19448_praise_night_tshirt_cannon'), 'D', 'Yes, because Lydia supplied the T-shirt cannon to a visibly intoxicated and inexperienced person.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is the only answer that is both true under the Gold Key and responsive to the duty call.', NULL, 'RC-TORTS-NE-001'),
  ('06eb07fa-94d9-5ccd-a02b-1cf6400c1acf', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19499_jericho_chariot_night'), 'A', 'Wharton’s Rule always bars a conspiracy charge whenever the target offense involves any agreement.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["two-party offense always bars conspiracy","profit motive decides Wharton''s Rule","all agreement crimes merge with conspiracy"]', 'The student reaches for a clean universal rule because the answer sounds decisive. The breaker is that always/whenever language over-expands a narrow doctrine.', 'The answer expands a narrow rule with always/whenever language.', 'Mark always/whenever and ask whether a narrow exception exists.', 'REM-CRIMINAL-WHARTON-COUNT'),
  ('d73013e2-8934-5bfa-8648-f351108fa5d2', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19499_jericho_chariot_night'), 'B', 'Wharton’s Rule bars the conspiracy charge only because the organizers hoped to make money from the event.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["two-party offense always bars conspiracy","profit motive decides Wharton''s Rule","all agreement crimes merge with conspiracy"]', 'The student treats profit as the reason the organizers matter. The breaker is that participant count, not payment, is the Wharton''s Rule axis.', 'The answer focuses on money rather than participant count.', 'Rename the axis as participant count, not compensation.', 'REM-CRIMINAL-WHARTON-COUNT'),
  ('6e0c87bc-e8e4-56ae-8d61-e229b2426a79', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19499_jericho_chariot_night'), 'C', 'Wharton’s Rule does not bar the charge because the agreement includes extra participants beyond the two racers needed for the offense.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'After the overclaim, payment red herring, and base-rule trap are cut, C is the only true-and-responsive answer.', NULL, 'REM-CRIMINAL-WHARTON-COUNT'),
  ('c8bbbc0c-9ef1-51fd-a73c-875c3d014dcc', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19499_jericho_chariot_night'), 'D', 'Wharton’s Rule bars the conspiracy charge because the illegal chariot race requires two racers.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["two-party offense always bars conspiracy","profit motive decides Wharton''s Rule","all agreement crimes merge with conspiracy"]', 'The student remembers the base Wharton''s Rule idea that a two-party offense can absorb conspiracy. The breaker is the extra-party exception when unnecessary organizers join the agreement.', 'The answer states the base two-party idea but omits the extra-party exception.', 'Apply the extra-party exception after counting actual participants.', 'REM-CRIMINAL-WHARTON-COUNT'),
  ('2689acb9-79f4-50e2-b51f-2ed6944b923c', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19502_manna_festival_finals_tax'), 'A', 'unconstitutional, because Congress violates the equal protection component of the Fifth Amendment by taxing final-round artisan food competitions while failing to tax other large paid food festivals.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["high_tax_is_unconstitutional","economic_harm_defeats_tax","all_similar_events_must_be_taxed","compelling_interest_always_helps"]', 'This sells the fairness instinct that if Congress taxes one large paid event category, it should tax neighboring paid event categories too. The breaker is the fabricated all-or-nothing tax rule; no suspect class or fundamental-right trigger appears.', 'The choice invents an all-or-nothing tax classification rule.', 'Require a protected trigger or a truly irrational classification before using equal protection to defeat a tax.', 'REM-CONLAW-TAX-REVENUE-01'),
  ('95624dd5-9994-5331-aaae-3db45e8d8a34', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19502_manna_festival_finals_tax'), 'B', 'unconstitutional, because a 40% admission tax is likely to reduce attendance at these final-round competitions and, therefore, is not rationally related to Congress’s legitimate interest in retiring disaster-recovery debt.', 0, '["contradiction"]', '["high_tax_is_unconstitutional","economic_harm_defeats_tax","all_similar_events_must_be_taxed","compelling_interest_always_helps"]', 'This sells the economic-impact worry that a high tax might shrink attendance and therefore look self-defeating. The breaker is the non sequitur; a paid-admission excise tax can still be rationally connected to revenue even if attendance drops.', 'The attendance-impact reason does not prove the tax lacks a revenue relationship.', 'Say: burdening the taxed activity is not the same as lacking a revenue relation.', 'REM-CONLAW-TAX-REVENUE-01'),
  ('60c304ff-51fe-5d61-9f51-5c5a39442f22', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19502_manna_festival_finals_tax'), 'C', 'constitutional, because an act of Congress that appears to be a revenue-raising measure on its face is not rendered invalid because it may have adverse economic consequences for the activity taxed.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It answers the precise tax-power call and uses the correct revenue-tax frame.', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-TAX-REVENUE-01'),
  ('f79bfa19-b20a-519d-be02-94cea4e43923', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19502_manna_festival_finals_tax'), 'D', 'constitutional, because the compelling national interest in retiring federal disaster-recovery debt justifies this tax as a temporary emergency measure.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["high_tax_is_unconstitutional","economic_harm_defeats_tax","all_similar_events_must_be_taxed","compelling_interest_always_helps"]', 'This sells the strongest-sounding constitutional vocabulary by pairing an emergency with a compelling national interest. The breaker is the wrong frame; the stem gives a revenue tax, not a strict-scrutiny trigger.', 'The choice imports strict-scrutiny language without a trigger.', 'Classify the claim home first: this is a tax-power item, not a heightened-scrutiny item.', 'REM-CONLAW-TAX-REVENUE-01'),
  ('f5b59a7a-0e86-5318-b42f-b137ab612e3f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19554_road_to_damascus_cashbox'), 'A', 'False pretenses, because the visitors handed the admission fees to Peter voluntarily.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["employee_theft_equals_embezzlement","voluntary_payment_equals_false_pretenses","permission_to_handle_defeats_theft"]', 'The student sees that visitors voluntarily handed money to Peter and treats the handoff as the classification. The breaker is that voluntary payment to the business is not title-by-deception to Peter.', 'False pretenses is the neighboring property-crime frame; the voluntary payment fact does not show title transferred to Peter by deception.', 'Ask whether the payer meant to transfer title to the worker personally.', 'RC-CRIM-CUSTODY-POSSESSION-01'),
  ('51cca9e0-2ba9-522c-ad15-dc7f43d29d43', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19554_road_to_damascus_cashbox'), 'B', 'No theft offense, because Peter was allowed to handle the admission money.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["employee_theft_equals_embezzlement","voluntary_payment_equals_false_pretenses","permission_to_handle_defeats_theft"]', 'The student focuses on Peter’s permission to touch and collect the money. The breaker is that permission to handle does not answer permission to keep.', 'Permission to handle the admission money does not answer permission to keep it.', 'Ask what the stem says the worker was allowed to do and what he actually did.', 'RC-CRIM-CUSTODY-POSSESSION-01'),
  ('91861b5b-99c4-5101-bbd0-a254c2d13fbb', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19554_road_to_damascus_cashbox'), 'C', 'Embezzlement, because all theft by a worker from the business is embezzlement.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["employee_theft_equals_embezzlement","voluntary_payment_equals_false_pretenses","permission_to_handle_defeats_theft"]', 'The student uses the familiar worker-theft-equals-embezzlement shortcut. The breaker is that all worker theft is too broad because custody-only workers can commit larceny.', 'All theft by a worker is too broad; worker status does not automatically produce embezzlement.', 'Circle all and classify by property path, not role.', 'RC-CRIM-CUSTODY-POSSESSION-01'),
  ('ba90cb80-5ac5-57bf-8bb6-69481f79e7cc', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19554_road_to_damascus_cashbox'), 'D', 'Larceny, because Peter had custody of the admission money while Lydia’s business retained possession.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'D is the only choice that answers the classification call and uses the custody/possession distinction required by the Gold Key.', NULL, 'RC-CRIM-CUSTODY-POSSESSION-01'),
  ('0f8d2bba-58f6-5290-b241-686142432c39', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19607_cana_hills_bethany_flats'), 'A', 'Strict scrutiny applies because the funding gap falls most heavily on low-income students, and low-income students are a suspect class.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","wrong_frame"]', '["education is fundamental","poverty is suspect","impact equals purpose","unfairness equals strict scrutiny"]', 'The choice makes the student’s inequality instinct do the work by treating low-income status as suspect. The breaker is that school-funding poverty or local wealth disparities do not trigger strict scrutiny under the Gold Key.', 'The choice treats low-income status as a suspect-class trigger for strict scrutiny.', 'Ask whether the claimed class is a recognized suspect class for this federal Equal Protection claim.', 'REM-CONLAW-TIER-TRIGGER-01'),
  ('263004ae-388e-5bc9-bc39-bc83e4b8519a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19607_cana_hills_bethany_flats'), 'B', 'Strict scrutiny applies because the disparity effectively denies students in the lower-tax-base district equal access to public education, which is a fundamental right.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","wrong_frame"]', '["education is fundamental","poverty is suspect","impact equals purpose","unfairness equals strict scrutiny"]', 'The choice feels right because education sounds too important to be reviewed deferentially. The breaker is the Gold Key that public education is not a federal fundamental right in this school-funding Equal Protection setting.', 'The choice treats public education as a federal fundamental right in a school-funding case.', 'Recall that Rodriguez places local-property-tax school funding in rational basis review.', 'REM-CONLAW-TIER-TRIGGER-01'),
  ('40c6f10e-0bad-51cd-baaa-3ccbd9c5816d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19607_cana_hills_bethany_flats'), 'C', 'Intermediate scrutiny applies because the facially neutral funding plan systematically disadvantages lower-income districts that substantially overlap with racial-minority communities.', 0, '["half_truth","wrong_frame"]', '["education is fundamental","poverty is suspect","impact equals purpose","unfairness equals strict scrutiny"]', 'The choice converts racial overlap and unequal effects into a heightened-scrutiny trigger. The breaker is that disparate impact alone is not enough without discriminatory purpose or a racial classification.', 'The choice gives impact and racial overlap, but not discriminatory purpose or a racial classification.', 'Ask whether the stem gives discriminatory purpose or a facial racial classification.', 'REM-CONLAW-TIER-TRIGGER-01'),
  ('571b16ef-9e89-5eb8-aeb5-36d5ffd2aea4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19607_cana_hills_bethany_flats'), 'D', 'Rational basis review applies, and the plan likely survives because local control of public schools and tying local tax revenue to local school spending are conceivable legitimate government interests.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'After the invalid heightened-review triggers are cut by Gold Keys, only the default-tier answer remains.', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-TIER-TRIGGER-01'),
  ('54a6dc21-f58b-50c0-9146-9b4ed23f2f20', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19721_jonah_whale_float'), 'A', 'Grant the motion, because a court would be unlikely to award more than $75,000 in damages on these facts.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","procedural_frame"]', '["notice_is_always_enough","unlikely_damages_defeat_jurisdiction","false_imprisonment_can_be_negligent","grant_result_is_enough"]', 'This choice gives the same grant result and makes the damages feel too speculative. The breaker is that likely recovery is not the amount-in-controversy standard and not the claim-sufficiency defect.', 'This invents a likely-recovery amount-in-controversy standard and does not resolve the claim-sufficiency defect.', 'Ask whether the reason is the actual motion defect.', 'REM-CIV-12B6-INTENT-01'),
  ('28d18d6e-a9e9-5508-a2fc-626917501c2b', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19721_jonah_whale_float'), 'B', 'Deny the motion, because there is no indication that it is impossible for recovery to exceed $75,000.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","procedural_frame"]', '["notice_is_always_enough","unlikely_damages_defeat_jurisdiction","false_imprisonment_can_be_negligent","grant_result_is_enough"]', 'This choice states the amount-in-controversy frame students remember from diversity jurisdiction. The breaker is that the motion is granted because the complaint fails to state false imprisonment, not because federal jurisdiction is missing.', 'This uses the amount-in-controversy frame when the operative defect is failure to state false imprisonment.', 'Separate jurisdiction survival from claim survival.', 'REM-CIV-12B6-INTENT-01'),
  ('fdc75a02-5a16-59ad-9548-63c02316b2b4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19721_jonah_whale_float'), 'C', 'Grant the motion, because the complaint fails to state a claim.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'After the anchor-assisted cuts, C is the only answer true and responsive to the motion.', NULL, 'REM-CIV-12B6-INTENT-01'),
  ('07377504-81ea-553e-9418-3b907009e5b4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19721_jonah_whale_float'), 'D', 'Deny the motion, because the complaint gives MannaJoy notice of the claim being asserted.', 0, '["wrong_element","procedural_frame"]', '["notice_is_always_enough","unlikely_damages_defeat_jurisdiction","false_imprisonment_can_be_negligent","grant_result_is_enough"]', 'This choice leans on the familiar notice-pleading idea. The breaker is that notice does not cure a complaint that pleads facts defeating the selected claim.', 'This supplies notice but does not answer the complaint-negates-element problem.', 'Ask whether notice also shows entitlement to relief.', 'REM-CIV-12B6-INTENT-01'),
  ('6d89cb36-7f9d-528b-ab51-f26bcd1ee94d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19793_dove_candle_ledgers'), 'A', 'Yes, because any discovery order that deals with a side issue instead of the merits is immediately appealable.', 0, '["half_truth","procedural_frame"]', '["cost_creates_appeal","separate_prong_enough","no_immediate_appeal_means_never"]', 'The student recognizes that collateral-order doctrine deals with issues separate from the merits. The breaker is that one prong is not the whole appealability gate.', 'It treats separateness from the merits as enough and omits the narrowness/effective-unreviewability gate.', 'Say: one prong is not the test.', 'RC-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-COLLATERAL-ORDER-NARROWNESS-01'),
  ('1e30c264-0043-5dcc-abc2-1bd5da172b7a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19793_dove_candle_ledgers'), 'B', 'No, because an ordinary document-production order usually must wait for final-judgment review.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is the best answer. The order is an ordinary document-production order. The fact that retrieving and scanning the documents will cost money does not make the order immediately appealable.

Gold Key: Collateral-order review is narrow. A discovery order must fit the small class of orders that are effectively unreviewable after final judgment; ordinary discovery-cost complaints do not.

Silver Key: In an appealability array, read the fight as review now vs review later. Cut the extreme “any/every/never/automatically” answers first, then ask whether final-judgment review is enough.', NULL, 'RC-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-COLLATERAL-ORDER-NARROWNESS-01'),
  ('8146b47d-6116-5dd3-ab64-404663b6f086', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19793_dove_candle_ledgers'), 'C', 'No, because a discovery order can never be challenged by any route.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","procedural_frame"]', '["cost_creates_appeal","separate_prong_enough","no_immediate_appeal_means_never"]', 'The student knows ordinary discovery orders usually are not appealable now and overcorrects. The breaker is that no immediate appeal does not mean no challenge by any route.', 'It says discovery orders can never be challenged, turning no immediate appeal into no review by any route.', 'Say: not now is not never.', 'RC-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-COLLATERAL-ORDER-NARROWNESS-01'),
  ('62208e9a-491a-5408-a6d4-e07e7673ae2d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19793_dove_candle_ledgers'), 'D', 'Yes, because an expensive production order automatically qualifies as a collateral order.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","procedural_frame"]', '["cost_creates_appeal","separate_prong_enough","no_immediate_appeal_means_never"]', 'The student treats expense as a fairness reason for immediate appellate protection. The breaker is that cost does not automatically satisfy collateral-order narrowness.', 'It says expense automatically creates a collateral order.', 'Say: cost is bait; gate first.', 'RC-CIVIL_PROCEDURE-COLLATERAL-ORDER-NARROWNESS-01'),
  ('7d345ffb-7f7d-5d30-9e78-147e94826664', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19840_red_sea_bridge_bolts'), 'A', 'Yes, unless Lydia''s lawyer later states the name in open court.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["everything_told_to_lawyer_is_secret","civil_cases_have_no_privilege","waiver_controls_all_privilege_questions"]', 'The choice sells a waiver story because lawyers repeating facts in court sounds like the moment a privilege would be lost. The breaker is that the asked-for item is an underlying fact, so waiver timing is not the question.', 'The choice answers a later waiver problem, not whether the underlying name was privileged when requested.', 'Circle the asserted ground in the stem and reject events not in the stem.', 'CIV-DISC-PRIV-01'),
  ('d2ca90dc-0b8c-5f8f-aee7-f8249d55edd0', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19840_red_sea_bridge_bolts'), 'B', 'No, because attorney-client privilege never applies in civil cases.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["everything_told_to_lawyer_is_secret","civil_cases_have_no_privilege","waiver_controls_all_privilege_questions"]', 'The choice sells an easy no by using a broad civil-case shortcut. The breaker is the absolute never, which contradicts the privilege frame rather than answering the fact-versus-communication split.', 'The word never overclaims by erasing civil attorney-client privilege.', 'Test both halves: the outcome may be right while the reason is overbroad.', 'CIV-DISC-PRIV-01'),
  ('7983325e-6a2d-55c4-858f-e188caed49b1', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19840_red_sea_bridge_bolts'), 'C', 'Yes, because every fact a client discusses with a lawyer while seeking legal advice becomes privileged.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["everything_told_to_lawyer_is_secret","civil_cases_have_no_privilege","waiver_controls_all_privilege_questions"]', 'The choice sells privacy because the fact was discussed with a lawyer during a legal-advice meeting. The breaker is the word every, which tries to convert all discussed facts into protected material.', 'The phrase every fact overextends privilege from communications to underlying facts.', 'Ask whether the request seeks the fact itself or the lawyer conversation.', 'CIV-DISC-PRIV-01'),
  ('d782465f-6a41-5eff-bca9-88033853dd18', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '19840_red_sea_bridge_bolts'), 'D', 'No, because an opposing party may discover relevant underlying facts even if those facts were communicated to counsel.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is the only choice that says no for the fact-versus-communication reason.', NULL, 'CIV-DISC-PRIV-01'),
