  ('83f79ca3-9694-5bbf-8f5f-09a7a72fc630', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20100_fish_and_loaves_keychains'), 'A', 'Barnabas may enforce the contract for all 2,400 keychains if the market price proves that the larger quantity was commercially reasonable.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["admission_of_contract_equals_all_terms","quantity_dispute_voids_everything","market_reasonableness_can_supply_quantity"]', 'The student sees commercial reasonableness as a practical way to validate the seller''s larger number. The breaker is that market reasonableness is not the admission-exception cap.', 'Market reasonableness is a fabricated expansion yardstick for the UCC admission exception.', 'Ask what number Lydia actually admitted.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-SOF-ADMISSION-QUANTITY-CAP'),
  ('525c70b3-fce1-514f-b02a-48ed978b7b4e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20100_fish_and_loaves_keychains'), 'B', 'The contract is enforceable under the admission exception only up to the 750 keychains Lydia admitted.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. Lydia admitted only 750 keychains. Gold Key: the UCC admission exception can satisfy the Statute of Frauds, but it caps enforcement at the quantity admitted. Silver Key: in an all / none / admitted-quantity array, lock the admitted number before reading the legal labels. The answer that lands exactly on 750 is the only answer that respects both the admission and the cap.', NULL, 'REM-CONTRACTS-SOF-ADMISSION-QUANTITY-CAP'),
  ('7582ab46-5fdd-5716-aff7-07eab670df02', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20100_fish_and_loaves_keychains'), 'C', 'Barnabas may enforce the contract for all 2,400 keychains because Lydia admitted that some contract existed.', 0, '["extreme_of_range"]', '["admission_of_contract_equals_all_terms","quantity_dispute_voids_everything","market_reasonableness_can_supply_quantity"]', 'The student treats Lydia''s admission that some contract existed as enough to enforce the entire alleged deal. The breaker is that the admission exception stops at the quantity admitted.', 'The choice overextends admission of some contract to all alleged goods.', 'Treat contract existence and admitted quantity as separate slots.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-SOF-ADMISSION-QUANTITY-CAP'),
  ('d5bccf0d-cbaf-5afd-957b-e1dc54a191fa', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20100_fish_and_loaves_keychains'), 'D', 'Barnabas may enforce none of the contract because Lydia disputes the quantity.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["admission_of_contract_equals_all_terms","quantity_dispute_voids_everything","market_reasonableness_can_supply_quantity"]', 'The student focuses on the disputed 2,400 and concludes that the whole oral deal fails. The breaker is that Lydia admitted 750, so the result is not none.', 'The choice says none even though the buyer admitted 750.', 'Reject all-or-none framing when a middle number is admitted.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-SOF-ADMISSION-QUANTITY-CAP'),
  ('b250b9e3-592d-5484-b7ce-3a9fdd4e4634', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20123_prayer_card_threat_writers'), 'A', 'Humiliation from seeing her prayer card in the episode.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["misleading_equals_liability","embarrassment_equals_fault","technical_label_confusion","privacy_trade_libel_confusion"]', 'The choice feels sympathetic because humiliation is the obvious human harm from the false implication. The breaker is that the call asks for the publisher''s mental state, not Hannah''s reaction.', 'Humiliation is harm, not the publisher mental-state showing the call asks for.', 'Ask whose mind the answer describes.', 'REM-TORTS-FALSE-LIGHT-FAULT-01'),
  ('be7f6a03-e56b-5f65-8051-8110a6bcd5d0', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20123_prayer_card_threat_writers'), 'B', 'Special damages, because false light is a trade-libel tort.', 0, '["misfit","wrong_frame"]', '["misleading_equals_liability","embarrassment_equals_fault","technical_label_confusion","privacy_trade_libel_confusion"]', 'The choice sounds lawyerly because special damages and trade libel are technical labels. The breaker is that it changes the frame from false-light mental state to a damages/category issue.', 'Special damages and trade libel answer a different frame from the false-light mental-state call.', 'Return to the call and demand a mental-state showing.', 'REM-TORTS-FALSE-LIGHT-FAULT-01'),
  ('5c649bc9-396f-5ad8-8523-50b621474328', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20123_prayer_card_threat_writers'), 'C', 'Actual malice, shown by using the graphic despite knowing the threat-writer implication was false or seriously doubting it.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. The call asks for the mental-state showing that supports the false-light claim. The producers had a note saying Hannah’s prayer card was not connected to the threat letters, but they used the graphic anyway. Gold Key: In a public-concern false-light claim, the constitutional fault unlock is actual malice: knowledge of falsity or reckless disregard for truth. Silver Key: On a mental-state call, first cut choices about harm, damages, tort category, or no-fault liability; the answer must point to the publisher’s state of mind.', NULL, 'REM-TORTS-FALSE-LIGHT-FAULT-01'),
  ('9675fdd5-1866-5582-a6c0-fc48c8526834', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20123_prayer_card_threat_writers'), 'D', 'Strict liability, because the episode graphic was misleading.', 0, '["flat_misstatement"]', '["misleading_equals_liability","embarrassment_equals_fault","technical_label_confusion","privacy_trade_libel_confusion"]', 'The choice feels efficient because a misleading graphic seems enough for liability. The breaker is the Gold Key: public-concern false light requires constitutional fault, not strict liability.', 'Strict liability is defeated by the public-concern false-light actual-malice Gold Key.', 'Ask whether the answer supplies knowledge or reckless disregard.', 'REM-TORTS-FALSE-LIGHT-FAULT-01'),
  ('2ac2d392-07ea-5cfc-9c48-0cd24f71498e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20127_jericho_trumpet'), 'A', 'Yes, because a later warrant based on the statement cannot cure any constitutional violation.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["all_fruits_suppressed","warrant_cures_violation","voluntary_means_no_violation","statement_and_object_same_remedy"]', 'The warrant language makes the answer sound precise because students expect taint to require a cure. The breaker is that the call is not about curing the warning failure; it is about whether voluntary-statement physical fruit is suppressed.', 'The answer turns a narrow physical-fruit remedy call into an absolute warrant-cure rule.', 'Ask: is the prosecution offering the words or the object?', 'REM-CRIM-MIRANDA-FRUIT-01'),
  ('d451d230-8011-53c6-af8c-02de9369706f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20127_jericho_trumpet'), 'B', 'Yes, because all evidence derived from an unwarned statement is fruit of the poisonous tree.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["all_fruits_suppressed","warrant_cures_violation","voluntary_means_no_violation","statement_and_object_same_remedy"]', 'The all-fruits rule borrows the familiar poisonous-tree image and feels protective of Miranda. The breaker is the Gold Key: voluntary unwarned testimonial statements are treated differently from physical evidence found through them.', 'The answer overclaims by saying all evidence derived from an unwarned statement is suppressed.', 'Say: voluntary unwarned statement physical fruit generally comes in.', 'REM-CRIM-MIRANDA-FRUIT-01'),
  ('107743bc-1a36-5ca0-9c37-fb090195aa72', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20127_jericho_trumpet'), 'C', 'No, because Paul''s voluntary statement means there was no Miranda violation at all.', 0, '["backwards","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["all_fruits_suppressed","warrant_cures_violation","voluntary_means_no_violation","statement_and_object_same_remedy"]', 'The word voluntary feels like it should erase the Miranda problem. The breaker is the Silver Key: voluntariness changes the remedy layer, not the existence of the warning failure.', 'The answer points voluntariness at the wrong layer; voluntariness limits the remedy but does not erase the warning failure.', 'Say: voluntary affects derivative evidence; it does not erase the warning problem.', 'REM-CRIM-MIRANDA-FRUIT-01'),
  ('fc5b6092-fb6f-5578-a266-7409e12ef76d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20127_jericho_trumpet'), 'D', 'No, because physical evidence derived from a voluntary unwarned statement need not be suppressed.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only D is true and responsive to the suppression-of-physical-evidence call.', NULL, 'REM-CRIM-MIRANDA-FRUIT-01'),
  ('2e4bff14-630c-5a5e-8258-1e3a0d6b486b', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20153_lampstand_labs'), 'A', 'Yes, because education is solely a matter for the states.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["all_public_aid_to_religious_schools_invalid","education_is_states_only","taxpayers_never_have_standing","right_result_means_right_answer"]', 'Education feels local, so a states-only answer sounds constitutionally serious. The breaker is that solely overclaims against Congress''s spending power.', 'The states-only education reason overclaims. Spending-power doctrine kills it.', 'Apply spending-power Gold Key before accepting states-only language.', 'REM-CONLAW-LAMPSTAND-01'),
  ('6ab70a11-232b-5115-a1a9-d2df0fa84b6d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20153_lampstand_labs'), 'B', 'No, because the Act restricts the donated kits to secular educational use.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. The injunction should not issue because the statute is structured as a neutral educational-aid program: religious and secular private schools are treated alike, and the donated kits are restricted to secular educational use.

Gold Key: Neutral aid to religious and nonreligious private schools is not automatically an Establishment Clause violation when the program uses neutral criteria and restricts aid to secular, nonideological use. Silver Key: Do not pick by the Yes/No result alone; grade the “because.” C has the right result but a bad threshold reason. B gives the merits reason that fits the statute.

In *Mitchell v. Helms*, the Court upheld a similar school-aid program where materials and equipment went to religious and nonreligious schools under neutral criteria and the aid was restricted to secular, neutral, nonideological use. ([Justia Law][1])', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-LAMPSTAND-01'),
  ('98b1e622-619d-572a-bc49-0678e8562df3', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20153_lampstand_labs'), 'C', 'No, because Mary and Peter lack standing to challenge federal spending.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","procedural_frame"]', '["all_public_aid_to_religious_schools_invalid","education_is_states_only","taxpayers_never_have_standing","right_result_means_right_answer"]', 'Standing is a powerful threshold, and threshold answers often beat merits answers. The breaker is the Establishment Clause taxpayer-standing Gold Key.', 'The no-standing threshold is false for this Establishment Clause spending challenge.', 'Use the taxpayer-standing Gold Key; same result with false reason dies.', 'REM-CONLAW-LAMPSTAND-01'),
  ('c59fa8cd-26b2-565c-91a3-bf45ea033fb8', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20153_lampstand_labs'), 'D', 'Yes, because using public funds to buy equipment for religious private schools violates the Establishment Clause.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["all_public_aid_to_religious_schools_invalid","education_is_states_only","taxpayers_never_have_standing","right_result_means_right_answer"]', 'Public funds going to religious schools feels like the core Establishment Clause problem. The breaker is the neutral secular-use aid Gold Key.', 'The Establishment Clause answer overclaims by treating religious-school aid as automatically invalid.', 'Apply the neutral-aid Gold Key and ask whether the answer ignores the secular-use condition.', 'REM-CONLAW-LAMPSTAND-01'),
  ('9465526e-4029-58f8-9201-9c1675ca7ad5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20186_road_to_emmaus_royalty_ledgers'), 'A', 'Quash the subpoena automatically because presidential personal records can never be obtained by Congress.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["Congressional power is unlimited","Presidential records are categorically immune","Impeachment is the only congressional subpoena route"]', 'The student wants to protect presidential privacy and treats the office as categorically shielded. The breaker is the absolute phrase can never, which the Gold Key rejects.', 'The answer uses automatic immunity language: presidential personal records can never be obtained. The Gold Key rejects categorical immunity and routes the court to calibrated review.', 'Ask whether the answer gives a calibrated court task or an automatic result.', 'REM-CONLAW-20186-MAZARS-01'),
  ('1b4f31e2-9507-52b2-8ad3-b74e698afb6d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20186_road_to_emmaus_royalty_ledgers'), 'B', 'Enforce the subpoena only if the committee is conducting an impeachment inquiry.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["Congressional power is unlimited","Presidential records are categorically immune","Impeachment is the only congressional subpoena route"]', 'The student recognizes impeachment as a real congressional power and turns it into the only permissible frame. The breaker is the invented only-if threshold, because legislative-purpose subpoenas are not limited to impeachment.', 'The answer invents an impeachment-only gateway. The stem gives a legislative-purpose frame, and the Gold Key permits legislative inquiry outside impeachment subject to limits.', 'Separate impeachment investigations from legislative investigations; then apply the Gold Key.', 'REM-CONLAW-20186-MAZARS-01'),
  ('835e09c7-e341-5446-bd8f-a7af22d0f55f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20186_road_to_emmaus_royalty_ledgers'), 'C', 'Enforce the subpoena automatically because Congress has unlimited investigative power over presidential personal records.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["Congressional power is unlimited","Presidential records are categorically immune","Impeachment is the only congressional subpoena route"]', 'The student remembers that Congress has broad investigative power and lets that memory overexpand. The breaker is unlimited and automatically, which are overclaim tells in a separation-of-powers standard.', 'The answer uses unlimited and automatically. The Silver Key flags automatic extremes as traps in a court-task call.', 'Use the Silver Key: automatic extremes lose to calibrated court-task language.', 'REM-CONLAW-20186-MAZARS-01'),
  ('aa5bff19-12f1-55fa-90d9-9a8c669f7caa', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20186_road_to_emmaus_royalty_ledgers'), 'D', 'Evaluate whether the subpoena serves a valid legislative purpose and is appropriately tailored in light of separation-of-powers concerns.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only D is true and responsive after cutting the three automatic extremes.', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-20186-MAZARS-01'),
  ('eb03052a-00a9-5a22-a2e7-af801c5b2205', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20213_mercy_pool_reliction'), 'A', 'No private owner, because exposed land created by reliction must be auctioned before anyone owns it.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["state_owns_all_former_waterbeds","recession_direction_controls","auction_required_for_new_land"]', 'The answer sounds official because an auction feels like a clean way to allocate newly exposed land. The breaker is that the auction step is not the usual reliction rule.', 'The auction step is invented and fails once the reliction anchor is applied.', 'Cut added procedures that are not part of the reliction anchor.', 'RP-ANCHOR-RELICTION-01'),
  ('8d513bbf-30f8-5aeb-baa2-c710b1c55382', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20213_mercy_pool_reliction'), 'B', 'Ruth, because gradual reliction generally shifts the water-boundary and adds the exposed land to the adjoining littoral parcel.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only B answers who owns the exposed land using the trigger facts.', NULL, 'RP-ANCHOR-RELICTION-01'),
  ('123b1145-93c0-55aa-894a-b673697db0d5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20213_mercy_pool_reliction'), 'C', 'The state, because all land once covered by Mercy Pool remains public forever.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["state_owns_all_former_waterbeds","recession_direction_controls","auction_required_for_new_land"]', 'The answer leans on the public-water instinct and sounds safe because the land was once under water. The breaker is the all/forever overclaim, which the reliction anchor defeats.', 'The all/forever wording overclaims and the reliction anchor supplies the exception.', 'Treat all/forever as an overclaim and apply the reliction Gold Key.', 'RP-ANCHOR-RELICTION-01'),
  ('70db0b87-b562-5869-a6c8-1870cfa84c47', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20213_mercy_pool_reliction'), 'D', 'Barnabas, because Mercy Pool receded in the direction of his far-side land.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","wrong_frame"]', '["state_owns_all_former_waterbeds","recession_direction_controls","auction_required_for_new_land"]', 'The answer gives Barnabas a plausible directional story because the water retreated toward the far side. The breaker is that ownership follows adjacency to the exposed land, not the direction of retreat.', 'The choice uses direction of recession instead of adjacency to the exposed strip.', 'Ask which parcel adjoins the exposed strip.', 'RP-ANCHOR-RELICTION-01'),
  ('c4371f23-fd47-5142-9338-d1ad06136e84', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20231_crown_above_caesars'), 'A', 'The law is invalid only if it also violates the Establishment Clause.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["rational_basis_saves_belief_ban","free_exercise_only_for_churches","establishment_required_for_religion_claim"]', 'The Establishment Clause sounds like the safest religion-clause answer. The breaker is the word only, because Free Exercise itself resolves punishment of belief.', 'The answer makes an Establishment Clause violation an only-if gate even though Free Exercise itself answers punishment of religious belief.', 'Ask whether Free Exercise alone answers punishment of religious belief.', 'REM-CONLAW-BELIEF-CONDUCT-01'),
  ('90534a9a-0554-561f-8fb3-15fe6687097d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20231_crown_above_caesars'), 'B', 'The law is valid if the state has a rational basis for deterring unlawful acts committed under the creed.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["rational_basis_saves_belief_ban","free_exercise_only_for_churches","establishment_required_for_religion_claim"]', 'The state’s conduct argument sounds practical and familiar. The breaker is that the statute punishes holding or teaching the creed, not unlawful acts.', 'The answer switches from the statute''s object, holding or teaching a creed, to unlawful acts committed under the creed.', 'Circle the punished object: hold or teach the creed.', 'REM-CONLAW-BELIEF-CONDUCT-01'),
  ('81c689eb-2182-58b3-95eb-32dbebf3a3d8', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20231_crown_above_caesars'), 'C', 'The law is unconstitutional because the government may not punish religious belief as such.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. Gold Key: Free Exercise draws a hard line between religious belief as such and religiously motivated conduct. The state may sometimes regulate conduct, but this statute reaches the creed itself: it criminalizes holding or teaching the belief. Silver Key: Lock the object of the statute before reading the choices. If the statute punishes belief, an answer about unlawful acts is answering the adjacent conduct question.', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-BELIEF-CONDUCT-01'),
  ('e5b97041-abd7-5a99-8e29-9a1d4adf245f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20231_crown_above_caesars'), 'D', 'The law is valid because the Free Exercise Clause protects only formal church organizations.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["rational_basis_saves_belief_ban","free_exercise_only_for_churches","establishment_required_for_religion_claim"]', 'The answer makes Free Exercise sound like an institutional church rule. The breaker is that individuals can hold and profess protected religious beliefs.', 'The answer over-narrows Free Exercise protection to formal church organizations.', 'Recall the Gold Key that Free Exercise protects belief/profession, including by individuals.', 'REM-CONLAW-BELIEF-CONDUCT-01'),
  ('7854be75-8c61-5ae0-ae7e-4d4c75c0ae04', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20247_bible_memory_kit'), 'A', 'Yes, because Rule 54(b) applies automatically in every multi-party civil case.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","procedural_frame"]', '["one_party_dismissed_equals_final","rule_applies_automatically","civil_rule_as_criminal_rule"]', 'The student sees multiple parties and reaches for a shortcut that sounds efficient. The breaker is that “automatically in every” overstates a procedural exception.', 'The choice turns Rule 54(b) into an automatic every-case shortcut.', 'Circle absolute words in procedural-rule answers.', 'CIV-REM-54B-CERT-GATE'),
  ('e14e9690-283a-5067-8201-66d655ae1727', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20247_bible_memory_kit'), 'B', 'No, because the court did not expressly direct entry of judgment or determine that there is no just reason for delay.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is the only answer that accounts for both missing Rule 54(b) requirements.', NULL, 'CIV-REM-54B-CERT-GATE'),
  ('0d0e1d5c-6cf7-5d96-a8b3-dd2df11882f6', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20247_bible_memory_kit'), 'C', 'No, because Rule 54(b) applies only to criminal cases.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","wrong_frame"]', '["one_party_dismissed_equals_final","rule_applies_automatically","civil_rule_as_criminal_rule"]', 'The student treats the rule number as a free-floating label instead of keeping the civil-procedure lane. The breaker is that the case is a federal civil action, not a criminal case.', 'The choice puts a civil procedure rule in a criminal-only frame.', 'Match the answer’s frame to the stem’s case type.', 'CIV-REM-54B-CERT-GATE'),
  ('568247f2-a08c-56de-9c8a-b1ce83851819', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20247_bible_memory_kit'), 'D', 'Yes, because one defendant is fully dismissed.', 0, '["wrong_element","procedural_frame"]', '["one_party_dismissed_equals_final","rule_applies_automatically","civil_rule_as_criminal_rule"]', 'The student locks onto the strongest fact: one defendant is fully dismissed. The breaker is that full dismissal is not the whole Rule 54(b) gate.', 'The choice gives a true partial-disposition fact but skips the Rule 54(b) certification gate.', 'Ask whether the answer accounts for both missing Rule 54(b) signals.', 'CIV-REM-54B-CERT-GATE'),
  ('11ed4c4f-0819-53b5-a17b-f4461a20c901', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20258_psalter_pressure'), 'A', 'Yes, because investigators may use any deception during interrogation.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["Miranda warnings automatically make confession admissible","police may use any deception","a written waiver is always required","a no answer is safe even with the wrong reason"]', 'The student remembers that police deception is often permitted in interrogation. The breaker is the absolute word any plus the stem’s added coercive pressure facts.', 'The choice says investigators may use any deception. The word any makes the statement too broad for a stem with coercive threats and deprivation.', 'Mark any, then compare the answer to the pressure facts.', 'CRIM-REM-20258-01'),
  ('d59b995e-6caf-5292-99f0-c92fe3df4f79', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20258_psalter_pressure'), 'B', 'No, because the investigators’ coercive threats and interrogation conditions rendered the confession involuntary.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. Gold Key: A Miranda warning is not a force field around a later confession. If officers use coercive threats and conditions that overbear the suspect’s will, the confession is involuntary and cannot be used in the prosecution’s case-in-chief.

Silver Key: Do not stop at the first clean procedure fact. The stem gives warnings first, then gives family-threat and deprivation facts. The answer must account for those pressure facts.', NULL, 'CRIM-REM-20258-01'),
  ('709d9634-116e-569e-8d91-92fb16790b47', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20258_psalter_pressure'), 'C', 'No, but only because Martha did not sign a written waiver form.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["Miranda warnings automatically make confession admissible","police may use any deception","a written waiver is always required","a no answer is safe even with the wrong reason"]', 'The student likes a clean paperwork defect because it sounds objective. The breaker is that the case turns on coercion, not a signed form.', 'The choice treats a missing signed waiver as the only defect. The form is not the gate; voluntariness is.', 'Ask whether the stated reason is the reason the stem was built to test.', 'CRIM-REM-20258-01'),
  ('b1f1f5b2-2604-5209-a574-c95af747a439', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20258_psalter_pressure'), 'D', 'Yes, because Martha received and understood Miranda warnings before confessing.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["Miranda warnings automatically make confession admissible","police may use any deception","a written waiver is always required","a no answer is safe even with the wrong reason"]', 'The student sees Miranda warnings and treats them as the whole admissibility answer. The breaker is that warnings do not answer whether later coercion overbore the suspect’s will.', 'The choice answers the Miranda warning layer. The call turns on whether the confession can be used after coercive pressure.', 'Treat warnings as one layer, then ask whether any later fact defeats admissibility.', 'CRIM-REM-20258-01'),
  ('3e017b1e-5b9c-5433-af7f-7a109d1d5336', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20271_lantern_handbell_evening'), 'A', '$17,000, because Daniel recovers the profit he would have earned after subtracting costs saved.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A is correct. Daniel’s expectation recovery is the benefit of the bargain, not the gross contract price and not the costs he never had to spend. The contract price was $48,000. The performance costs Daniel avoided were $31,000. His expected net profit was therefore $17,000.

Gold Key: In a service contract repudiated before performance, expectation damages are the contractor’s lost profit when all performance costs are avoided: contract price minus costs saved, plus any other proven loss.

Silver Key: Read the answer array as a damages-measure array: gross price, expected cost, net profit, and zero. The only answer that both uses the contract price and subtracts the avoided costs survives.', NULL, 'REM-CONTRACTS-EXPECTATION-SAVED-COSTS-01'),
  ('9338620b-4b0e-5881-bd3b-1521d0c2f503', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20271_lantern_handbell_evening'), 'B', '$48,000, because Lydia repudiated the contract before Daniel began preparing.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["gross price equals damages","expected costs equal damages","no work means no loss"]', 'The contract price is the easiest number to grab after seeing a repudiation. The breaker is that the stem says every performance cost was avoided, so gross price overpays.', 'The choice uses the gross contract price but ignores the visible saved-cost fact.', 'Mark the price as a gross input, then subtract avoided costs.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-EXPECTATION-SAVED-COSTS-01'),
  ('b0fd796c-1d7b-52f1-8a8d-cce77d43eb4a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20271_lantern_handbell_evening'), 'C', 'Nothing, because Daniel had not yet begun preparing when Lydia repudiated.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["gross price equals damages","expected costs equal damages","no work means no loss"]', 'The no-work fact feels like no loss because Daniel never started. The breaker is the profit he lost when Lydia canceled before he could earn it.', 'The choice invents a no-work prerequisite for lost-profit recovery.', 'Apply the Gold Key: pre-performance repudiation can still destroy profit.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-EXPECTATION-SAVED-COSTS-01'),
  ('bfe4300e-eb5e-54aa-bcdd-f52b4345c059', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20271_lantern_handbell_evening'), 'D', '$31,000, because Daniel expected to spend that amount performing.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["gross price equals damages","expected costs equal damages","no work means no loss"]', 'The expected cost number looks precise and appears in the stem. The breaker is that avoided cost is subtracted, not paid as the recovery.', 'The choice uses the expected-cost number as the recovery, but the stem says that cost was avoided.', 'Ask whether the number should be added, subtracted, or ignored.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-EXPECTATION-SAVED-COSTS-01'),
  ('3b789615-ef21-59e5-b400-984d230198ac', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20291_nativity_prop_rental_freeze'), 'A', 'No, because orders that operate as injunctions can never be appealed before final judgment.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","procedural_frame"]', '["all_interlocutory_orders_wait","order_label_controls","all_management_orders_appealable"]', 'Final-judgment language feels safe because most appeals wait until the end. The Gold Key breaks it because injunction-effect orders are a named immediate-appeal lane.', 'The final-judgment idea is overextended by the word never.', 'Mark never, then recall the injunction immediate-appeal Gold Key.', 'CIV-REM-20291-FUNCTIONAL-INJUNCTION'),
  ('923cfb63-f6f2-584f-9ecc-82048c9b3ab9', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20291_nativity_prop_rental_freeze'), 'B', 'No, because an order is immediately appealable only if it is labeled “injunction.”', 0, '["tiered_absolute","procedural_frame"]', '["all_interlocutory_orders_wait","order_label_controls","all_management_orders_appealable"]', 'Caption language feels technical because courts often care about order names. The Gold Key and Silver Key break it because this trap asks for labels when the command does the work.', 'The caption-only rule uses the word only to create a magic-word requirement.', 'Read the operative verb: Ruth may not rent until trial.', 'CIV-REM-20291-FUNCTIONAL-INJUNCTION'),
  ('affd74e9-e9d5-5b29-8ede-8cc3eace71ec', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20291_nativity_prop_rental_freeze'), 'C', 'Yes, because the order commands Ruth to stop doing something before trial and operates as an injunction.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. The order does more than manage deadlines or organize discovery. It tells Ruth to stop renting specific property until trial. Gold Key: for injunction appealability, the legal name of the order is not controlling; the order’s practical effect is. Silver Key: do not read the caption first; read the verb. “Do not rent” is a stop-command, so the order operates like an injunction.', NULL, 'CIV-REM-20291-FUNCTIONAL-INJUNCTION'),
  ('afc7cf3e-7d9e-5fbf-bd31-c7ba9116546b', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20291_nativity_prop_rental_freeze'), 'D', 'Yes, because every trial-preparation protocol is immediately appealable.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","procedural_frame"]', '["all_interlocutory_orders_wait","order_label_controls","all_management_orders_appealable"]', 'Trial-management labels make the order sound procedural and harmless. The breaker is the word every, which turns one functionally coercive order into a universal appealability rule.', 'The word every makes all protocols immediately appealable, which is broader than the call and the rule.', 'Cut every; ask why this protocol is special.', 'CIV-REM-20291-FUNCTIONAL-INJUNCTION'),
  ('c5d17cdb-2b2f-5e27-ba67-1e33aa4d46a4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20307_bethany_banners_transcript'), 'A', 'Admitted as a statement by Bethany Banners''s employee on a matter within the scope of employment, with the transcript admitted as a public record.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A is correct. The transcript is a two-layer evidence item. The first layer is Peter’s earlier testimony, offered for its truth. Gold Key: in a transcript problem, each hearsay layer needs its own path. Peter’s statement concerns his work for Bethany Banners and was made while he was still employed, so it can be used against Bethany Banners as an employee/opposing-party statement. The second layer is the court transcript itself. A court transcript records what was said in court as part of an official court function, so the transcript layer fits the public-record path.

Silver Key: split the answer into two layers before you pick an exception name. One choice must account for both the speaker’s statement and the transcript that carries it. A is the only answer that does that.', NULL, 'REMED-EVIDENCE-DOUBLE-HEARSAY-TRANSCRIPT'),
  ('eac93b1d-97d6-58ce-9e2a-e5ee60026e93', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20307_bethany_banners_transcript'), 'B', 'Admitted under the recorded recollection exception to the hearsay rule.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["all_prior_testimony_is_former_testimony","all_written_records_are_recorded_recollection","hearsay_means_automatic_exclusion"]', 'The choice sees a written record and reaches for a record-style hearsay exception. The breaker is that this is a court transcript, not the employee''s adopted memory record.', 'Recorded recollection is a true Evidence category, but this transcript is not Peter''s adopted memory record.', 'Ask whether the witness made or adopted the record as a memory aid.', 'REMED-EVIDENCE-DOUBLE-HEARSAY-TRANSCRIPT'),
  ('d687b599-6cf7-5058-abf6-9143a73a3467', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20307_bethany_banners_transcript'), 'C', 'Excluded as hearsay not within any exception or exclusion.', 0, '["half_truth"]', '["all_prior_testimony_is_former_testimony","all_written_records_are_recorded_recollection","hearsay_means_automatic_exclusion"]', 'The choice correctly senses a hearsay problem and gives the safe-sounding exclusion answer. The breaker is that multiple hearsay is not automatically excluded when each layer has a path.', 'The answer identifies hearsay but omits the available paths for each layer.', 'For every transcript, ask what admits the speaker''s statement and what admits the transcript.', 'REMED-EVIDENCE-DOUBLE-HEARSAY-TRANSCRIPT'),
  ('72caea9a-2639-54e1-a3bf-aa21e32bfbb5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20307_bethany_banners_transcript'), 'D', 'Admitted under the former testimony exception to the hearsay rule.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["all_prior_testimony_is_former_testimony","all_written_records_are_recorded_recollection","hearsay_means_automatic_exclusion"]', 'The choice sees earlier sworn testimony and reaches for the familiar former-testimony exception. The breaker is that the current opponent did not have the required earlier opportunity and motive to examine.', 'Former testimony is the wrong context because the current civil defendant did not examine Peter in the earlier criminal case.', 'Ask whether the current opponent had the prior chance and similar motive to examine.', 'REMED-EVIDENCE-DOUBLE-HEARSAY-TRANSCRIPT'),
  ('fc90baf7-ad87-52e5-abe0-59e831568274', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20310_psalms_wax_lamp'), 'A', 'It may matter only to feasibility if feasibility is genuinely disputed, but it does not replace the breach analysis.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A is correct. The later wire guard does not answer the breach question by itself. The breach question still asks whether reasonable care required the guard before Ruth was burned. Gold Key: a later safety change is not proof that the earlier condition was negligent; its limited use is a non-breach purpose such as feasibility, and only if that purpose is genuinely disputed. Silver Key: lock the call to “best use for breach.” Do not let the later fix become a shortcut for deciding whether the earlier setup was unreasonable.', NULL, 'REM-TORTS-SRM-01'),
  ('a8b25f79-dd58-527d-b30a-705528064383', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20310_psalms_wax_lamp'), 'B', 'It proves Ruth was contributorily negligent because Lydia added the guard after the burn.', 0, '["wrong_element","wrong_frame"]', '["repair_equals_admission","later_means_irrelevant","plaintiff_fault_wrong_call"]', 'The answer sounds fault-focused, so it feels relevant in a negligence case. The breaker is that Ruth''s contributory negligence is not the breach question.', 'The answer shifts from Lydia''s breach to Ruth''s contributory negligence.', 'Ask whose conduct the call is testing.', 'REM-TORTS-SRM-01'),
  ('44759e27-c07e-5491-9bc5-486a5a64f3db', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20310_psalms_wax_lamp'), 'C', 'It conclusively proves Lydia breached her duty before Ruth was burned.', 0, '["extreme_of_range","offered_for_purpose"]', '["repair_equals_admission","later_means_irrelevant","plaintiff_fault_wrong_call"]', 'The answer sells the hindsight shortcut: Lydia fixed it later, so the earlier setup must have been careless. The breaker is the overclaim, because the later guard cannot conclusively prove breach.', 'The answer turns a later guard into conclusive proof of earlier breach.', 'Replace hindsight with the prior-condition breach question.', 'REM-TORTS-SRM-01'),
  ('2ceb64ac-ecdb-5d2b-9c0e-35a7d890e069', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20310_psalms_wax_lamp'), 'D', 'It is always irrelevant to every issue because it happened after the injury.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","offered_for_purpose"]', '["repair_equals_admission","later_means_irrelevant","plaintiff_fault_wrong_call"]', 'The answer sells a simple timing rule: after the injury means outside the case. The breaker is the absolute, because later measures are not always irrelevant to every issue.', 'The answer says later measures are always irrelevant to every issue.', 'Preserve limited uses while rejecting breach proof.', 'REM-TORTS-SRM-01'),
  ('36d151d5-a625-5973-b492-ad1c26f4192c', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20312_loaves_fishes_retreat'), 'A', 'Martha must pay the principal, and Stephen must pay the interest.', 0, '["backwards"]', '["current_possessor_pays_all","future_owner_pays_all","balanced_split_without_direction","rental_value_overread"]', 'The student sees a clean split and likes that each party pays one component. The breaker is that the split is reversed under the Gold Key.', 'The choice reverses the anchor allocation by putting principal on the life tenant and interest on the remainderman.', 'Apply Gold Key: life tenant interest; remainderman principal.', 'RP-REM-LIFE-ENCUMBRANCE-01'),
  ('eea6c959-1ccc-5c61-817f-215812e03dcb', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20312_loaves_fishes_retreat'), 'B', 'Stephen must pay both principal and interest.', 0, '["extreme_of_range"]', '["current_possessor_pays_all","future_owner_pays_all","balanced_split_without_direction","rental_value_overread"]', 'The student focuses on Stephen ultimately owning the parcel and gives him the whole mortgage burden. The breaker is that future ownership maps to principal, not interest.', 'The choice over-extends the remainderman''s principal burden to interest.', 'Assign only principal to the future-equity holder.', 'RP-REM-LIFE-ENCUMBRANCE-01'),
  ('06cb12df-36fd-5c96-bdd3-685a15b1d59c', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20312_loaves_fishes_retreat'), 'C', 'Martha must pay the interest, and Stephen must pay the principal.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only C assigns interest to the life tenant and principal to the remainderman.', NULL, 'RP-REM-LIFE-ENCUMBRANCE-01'),
  ('17c95413-d825-5626-9f61-5d45875d9153', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20312_loaves_fishes_retreat'), 'D', 'Martha must pay both principal and interest.', 0, '["extreme_of_range"]', '["current_possessor_pays_all","future_owner_pays_all","balanced_split_without_direction","rental_value_overread"]', 'The student focuses on Martha’s possession and the parcel’s rental value, then makes her pay everything. The breaker is that current possession maps to interest, not principal.', 'The choice over-extends the life tenant''s interest burden to principal.', 'Use rental value only for the life tenant’s interest burden.', 'RP-REM-LIFE-ENCUMBRANCE-01'),
  ('b397436b-7046-5bc6-8ae5-13e546707112', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20313_bethlehem_olivewood_crosses'), 'A', 'Yes, but only if the customers later fail to prove substantial need for the communications.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["fraud_topic_automatic_exception","substantial_need_overrides_privilege","advice_against_act_defeats_privilege"]', 'The student recognizes substantial need as a real discovery phrase and assumes it can defeat privilege. The breaker is that substantial need answers work-product, not attorney-client privilege.', 'Substantial need is a work-product idea, not the attorney-client privilege test.', 'Ask which protection the call names before applying any exception phrase.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-PRIV-CRIME-FRAUD-20313'),
  ('fd6830ed-a69f-56f6-be29-31ff37fc9651', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20313_bethlehem_olivewood_crosses'), 'B', 'No, because any discussion of a potentially fraudulent advertisement triggers the crime-fraud exception.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["fraud_topic_automatic_exception","substantial_need_overrides_privilege","advice_against_act_defeats_privilege"]', 'The student sees fraud-related subject matter and treats the exception as automatic. The breaker is that crime-fraud turns on purpose, not mere topic.', 'The word ''any'' overreads crime-fraud by making suspicious subject matter automatic.', 'Find the client-purpose sentence in the stem.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-PRIV-CRIME-FRAUD-20313'),
  ('e564fd37-9451-5503-9b79-01109fd69f35', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20313_bethlehem_olivewood_crosses'), 'C', 'Yes, because she sought confidential legal advice to determine and avoid unlawful conduct, not to further a fraud.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only C is true and responsive after the wrong-frame and overclaim traps are removed.', NULL, 'REM-EVIDENCE-PRIV-CRIME-FRAUD-20313'),
  ('fb448f2d-8e98-5b58-9e28-4936440595b2', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20313_bethlehem_olivewood_crosses'), 'D', 'No, because Paul ultimately advised against the advertisement.', 0, '["backwards"]', '["fraud_topic_automatic_exception","substantial_need_overrides_privilege","advice_against_act_defeats_privilege"]', 'The student treats the lawyer''s negative advice as a reason privilege should fail. The breaker is that advice against the act supports the compliance-advice route.', 'Advice against the act points toward compliance advice, not loss of privilege.', 'Ask whether the fact points toward compliance or wrongdoing.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-PRIV-CRIME-FRAUD-20313'),
  ('cf3279fd-ebef-5789-afc3-759670020e08', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20328_bethlehem_star_drop'), 'A', 'No, because hiring a rigging contractor always defeats Lydia''s responsibility for res ipsa.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["no_exact_defect_no_case","contractor_automatically_breaks_control","res_ipsa_equals_judgment"]', 'A student sees Timothy''s contractor role and assumes Lydia is out. The breaker is the absolute word always, plus Lydia''s retained operational responsibility.', 'The word always makes the contractor point an overclaim.', 'Circle always and look for retained responsibility facts.', 'RC-TORTS-RES-IPSA-01'),
  ('db8a3208-311f-54ce-b3ba-f3788f2b4317', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20328_bethlehem_star_drop'), 'B', 'No, because Martha cannot identify the precise rigging defect.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["no_exact_defect_no_case","contractor_automatically_breaks_control","res_ipsa_equals_judgment"]', 'A student thinks a negligence plaintiff must identify the precise mechanical failure. The breaker is the Gold Key that res ipsa can supply a circumstantial inference without direct defect proof.', 'It invents a precise-defect-proof requirement that the Gold Key defeats.', 'Say: res ipsa is the bridge when exact direct proof is missing.', 'RC-TORTS-RES-IPSA-01'),
  ('76f787e8-75ac-585f-9e77-00ab95b55ea5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20328_bethlehem_star_drop'), 'C', 'Yes, because res ipsa requires judgment for Martha once the overhead prop falls.', 0, '["extreme_of_range"]', '["no_exact_defect_no_case","contractor_automatically_breaks_control","res_ipsa_equals_judgment"]', 'A student recognizes res ipsa and overcorrects into a plaintiff win. The breaker is that res ipsa permits an inference rather than requiring judgment.', 'It pushes a permissible inference into required judgment.', 'Replace requires judgment with permits inference.', 'RC-TORTS-RES-IPSA-01'),
  ('1f5ea7bd-217e-5005-b1b3-4090be35a918', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20328_bethlehem_star_drop'), 'D', 'Yes, because the prop''s sudden drop during normal show use can support a negligence inference without direct defect proof.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A and C overclaim; B loses the Gold-Key fight on direct proof.', NULL, 'RC-TORTS-RES-IPSA-01'),
  ('6b778f9a-aecc-5c60-8d8d-17c58cdabe04', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20351_red_sea_mini_golf'), 'A', 'Grant rescission because hidden subsurface drainage defects are always outside an as-is clause.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["both_mistaken_means_rescission","hidden_defects_escape_as_is","risk_requires_actual_inspection"]', 'It sells the thought that hidden defects are too serious for an as-is clause to cover. The breaker is the word always, because the clause expressly names hidden defects.', 'The word always overclaims the effect of hidden-defect status.', 'Circle always and test whether the stem''s exact clause names the risk.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-RISK-BEFORE-RESCISSION-01'),
  ('658d417a-eec4-5c30-9b21-38d3a55e7680', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20351_red_sea_mini_golf'), 'B', 'Deny rescission only if Barnabas proves that Ruth personally inspected every drainage tunnel.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["both_mistaken_means_rescission","hidden_defects_escape_as_is","risk_requires_actual_inspection"]', 'It sells the idea that assumption of risk must be backed by personal inspection. The breaker is that the inspection requirement is invented.', 'The answer invents a personal-inspection prerequisite.', 'Ask whether the answer''s proof condition appears in the stem or a taught anchor.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-RISK-BEFORE-RESCISSION-01'),
  ('546b24c0-1e89-520c-980d-c66ade2b071d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20351_red_sea_mini_golf'), 'C', 'Grant rescission because both parties were mistaken about the drainage tunnels.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["both_mistaken_means_rescission","hidden_defects_escape_as_is","risk_requires_actual_inspection"]', 'It sells the true mutual-mistake fact and feels like the classic rule. The breaker is that it skips the as-is risk-allocation term.', 'The answer proves mutual mistake but omits risk allocation.', 'After confirming both parties were mistaken, ask who bore the mistake-risk.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-RISK-BEFORE-RESCISSION-01'),
  ('4c3097fd-1d69-5492-9ca0-5b63fecfe7a6', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20351_red_sea_mini_golf'), 'D', 'Deny rescission because Ruth expressly assumed the risk of hidden subsurface drainage defects.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only D is true and responsive after the Gold Key risk-allocation check.', NULL, 'REM-CONTRACTS-RISK-BEFORE-RESCISSION-01'),
  ('78a6edd5-1aac-5c42-ac27-0b6f5b32bba2', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20353_baptism_tank_burst'), 'A', 'No, because Section 1367(b) bars all low-value or nondiverse counterclaims by defendants in diversity cases.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["every_claim_must_exceed_75000","section_1367b_bars_all_low_value_claims","federal_question_is_any_federal_court_case","correct_result_wrong_reason"]', 'The student sees Section 1367(b) and assumes the specific statute must be the sophisticated answer. The breaker is that the answer expands plaintiff-side limits into an all-defendant-claim bar.', 'Over-expands Section 1367(b) into an all-defendant-counterclaim bar.', 'Say the Gold Key: defendant same-event counterclaims may ride supplemental jurisdiction.', 'CIV-REM-20353-DEFENDANT-COUNTERCLAIM'),
  ('4d8fc7e6-327e-5c9b-a1c7-c3c79fd8f612', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20353_baptism_tank_burst'), 'B', 'Yes, but only because the counterclaim presents a federal question.', 0, '["misfit","wrong_frame"]', '["every_claim_must_exceed_75000","section_1367b_bars_all_low_value_claims","federal_question_is_any_federal_court_case","correct_result_wrong_reason"]', 'The student senses the court can hear the counterclaim and accepts the first yes answer. The breaker is that no federal-law fact appears, so the yes reason is the wrong jurisdictional hook.', 'Uses a federal-question reason when the stem supplies a same-event supplemental-jurisdiction hook.', 'Ask whether the stem gives federal law; if not, use the same-event hook.', 'CIV-REM-20353-DEFENDANT-COUNTERCLAIM'),
  ('e6c5cbe3-380a-5217-ab9d-60efbe8637ae', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20353_baptism_tank_burst'), 'C', 'No, because each claim in a diversity case must independently exceed $75,000.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["every_claim_must_exceed_75000","section_1367b_bars_all_low_value_claims","federal_question_is_any_federal_court_case","correct_result_wrong_reason"]', 'The student remembers the $75,000 diversity threshold and applies it to every claim. The breaker is the word each, because supplemental jurisdiction can carry a related defendant counterclaim below the threshold.', 'Turns the diversity amount threshold into an every-claim independent-amount rule.', 'Separate the anchor diversity claim from a related counterclaim riding supplemental jurisdiction.', 'CIV-REM-20353-DEFENDANT-COUNTERCLAIM'),
  ('8cc726e4-ecee-5e7a-b9b8-ce1d16dee3c8', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20353_baptism_tank_burst'), 'D', 'Yes, because the counterclaim arises from the same burst and forms part of the same Article III case.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A and C overclaim; B answers a different jurisdictional hook; D alone is true and responsive.', NULL, 'CIV-REM-20353-DEFENDANT-COUNTERCLAIM'),
  ('c2bc7aac-6ec1-5760-98cc-073c2ac1ecdd', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20370_dove_mug_notice'), 'A', 'Paul, because a merchant buyer that accepts delivery of nonconforming goods is bound to pay for them at the contract price.', 0, '["half_truth","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["defect_alone_wins","acceptance_alone_erases_all_remedies","seller_inspection_controls_price_action"]', 'This choice reaches the seller-wins side and uses the real accepted-goods idea. The breaker is that acceptance alone is incomplete because timely notice can preserve defect remedies.', 'Same seller outcome, but acceptance alone is an incomplete reason because timely notice can preserve nonconformity remedies.', 'Force the same-outcome wrong-reason check: winner side is not enough; reason must match the trigger fact.', 'RC-CONTRACTS-NOTICE-AFTER-ACCEPTANCE-01'),
  ('95bbf7de-6c52-593c-9863-dba55794a3ed', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20370_dove_mug_notice'), 'B', 'Lydia, because a merchant seller is not entitled to the price of nonconforming goods if a reasonable inspection before shipment would have disclosed the nonconformity.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["defect_alone_wins","acceptance_alone_erases_all_remedies","seller_inspection_controls_price_action"]', 'This choice makes seller inspection sound like a fair commercial responsibility. The breaker is that it invents a price-action defense not supplied by the UCC notice path.', 'The seller-inspection condition is an invented bar to the price action.', 'Cut invented commercial-sounding requirements unless the rule or stem makes them controlling.', 'RC-CONTRACTS-NOTICE-AFTER-ACCEPTANCE-01'),
  ('7d877ce4-8302-59d9-9eef-b6f67b8cc4c3', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20370_dove_mug_notice'), 'C', 'Paul, because Lydia failed to notify him that the mugs were missing the gold dove decals.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. Lydia knew the mugs were missing the gold dove decals when Timothy reported the defect on delivery day. She did not notify Paul then. She also did not notify him when the invoice arrived more than a month later. She raised the defect only after Paul sued for the price.

Gold Key: When a buyer accepts goods and discovers a defect, the buyer must notify the seller of the breach within a reasonable time or lose the defect remedy. Silver Key: Do not pick the seller-wins choice just because it reaches the right side; in this array, the winning seller choice must use the notice fact, not acceptance alone.', NULL, 'RC-CONTRACTS-NOTICE-AFTER-ACCEPTANCE-01'),
  ('9e890eda-bc72-5836-9f8f-79d8e4643ed4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20370_dove_mug_notice'), 'D', 'Lydia, because the mugs did not conform to the contract of sale.', 0, '["wrong_element","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["defect_alone_wins","acceptance_alone_erases_all_remedies","seller_inspection_controls_price_action"]', 'This choice uses the most visible fact: the mugs did not match the order. The breaker is that the call asks whether Lydia preserved that defect defense after months of silence.', 'The defect is real, but the price-action call turns on whether Lydia preserved the remedy after discovering it.', 'Name the call: seller price action after buyer silence, not abstract nonconformity.', 'RC-CONTRACTS-NOTICE-AFTER-ACCEPTANCE-01'),
  ('f1aec1f9-5b92-5c44-bbb9-fb44113a5448', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20387_psalms_chess_indictment'), 'A', 'Grant the motion unless the prosecutor proves that the arresting officers acted in good faith.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["bad_arrest_erases_case","good_faith_applies_to_every_fourth_amendment_problem","rearrest_required_to_prosecute"]', 'The choice recognizes a familiar good-faith rescue from Fourth Amendment suppression doctrine. The breaker is that the call asks for dismissal and no arrest-derived evidence is being offered.', 'Good faith belongs to the suppression/admissibility lane; the call asks dismissal and no arrest-derived evidence is being offered.', 'Ask what the motion requests and whether any arrest-derived evidence is being offered.', 'CRIM-REM-ARREST-REMEDY-01'),
  ('ba33c5f2-5444-5483-a9cb-f9243d2cb53b', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20387_psalms_chess_indictment'), 'B', 'Deny the motion only if Peter was released and rearrested with a valid warrant.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["bad_arrest_erases_case","good_faith_applies_to_every_fourth_amendment_problem","rearrest_required_to_prosecute"]', 'The choice sells procedural cleanup by making a new valid arrest sound like a cure. The breaker is that independent evidence lets the prosecution proceed without rerunning the arrest.', 'The answer invents a release-and-rearrest prerequisite for prosecution on independent evidence.', 'Reject invented ''only if'' prerequisites unless the anchor supplies them.', 'CRIM-REM-ARREST-REMEDY-01'),
  ('b689b2a8-e7d4-5224-814c-aa621538c6ad', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20387_psalms_chess_indictment'), 'C', 'Grant the motion, because an unlawful arrest nullifies any later indictment.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["bad_arrest_erases_case","good_faith_applies_to_every_fourth_amendment_problem","rearrest_required_to_prosecute"]', 'The choice sells the moral shortcut that an illegal arrest poisons the whole case. The breaker is that the remedy targets tainted evidence, not the indictment itself.', 'The answer overclaims by making an unlawful arrest nullify any later indictment.', 'Name the remedy: suppression of tainted evidence, not automatic dismissal.', 'CRIM-REM-ARREST-REMEDY-01'),
  ('cc8baa12-b8ba-5a37-a20b-ef7979f3e758', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20387_psalms_chess_indictment'), 'D', 'Deny the motion, because an unlawful arrest does not require dismissal when the prosecution rests on evidence independent of the arrest.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'D is correct. The motion asks for dismissal of the indictment, not suppression of evidence. The arrest produced no statement and no physical evidence, and the prosecution is relying on video and shopper statements already in the file before the arrest.

Silver Key: Lock the remedy first. This is a dismissal question, not an evidence-admissibility question.

Gold Key: An unlawful arrest does not automatically erase a later prosecution. The criminal-case remedy targets evidence obtained through the illegality; a prosecution supported by independent evidence may proceed.', NULL, 'CRIM-REM-ARREST-REMEDY-01'),
  ('6a934738-9b45-5dcc-9673-c18e1b8e10c4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20404_acts_axes_cash_loads'), 'A', 'inadmissible, because financial records are always unfairly prejudicial in a civil theft case.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["evidence must be conclusive","damaging equals unfairly prejudicial","contradiction evidence is impeachment only"]', 'This choice sells the fear that money evidence will make the jury punish Stephen for being suspiciously flush with cash. The breaker is the absolute word always, which tries to turn a balancing question into an automatic exclusion.', 'The word always makes unfair prejudice automatic.', 'Replace automatic exclusion with a balancing frame.', 'EVI-REM-ANY-TENDENCY-01'),
  ('2d32d483-e314-5e04-bba4-5c0aa3a441fb', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20404_acts_axes_cash_loads'), 'B', 'admissible as circumstantial evidence that Stephen received funds from a source beyond his stated pay.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. The cash-load records are admissible because they make Mary’s claim more probable: Stephen said he received only $3,200 for the season, while the records show $18,600 in same-season cash loads. Gold Key: relevance is an “any tendency” threshold, not a conclusive-proof requirement. Silver Key: in a relevance array, cut answers that demand “conclusive,” “always,” or “only”; the surviving answer states what the evidence tends to show. Stephen may argue gifts or family loans, but that attacks weight, not admissibility.', NULL, 'EVI-REM-ANY-TENDENCY-01'),
  ('064a7d3c-6902-52a9-9b66-035f3166cea1', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20404_acts_axes_cash_loads'), 'C', 'inadmissible, because the cash loads do not conclusively prove Stephen took Mary’s receipts.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["evidence must be conclusive","damaging equals unfairly prejudicial","contradiction evidence is impeachment only"]', 'This choice sells a certainty instinct: if the cash could be gifts or loans, it feels too weak to admit. The breaker is that relevance asks for tendency, not conclusive proof.', 'The choice invents a conclusive-proof threshold.', 'Ask whether the evidence makes a consequential fact more probable.', 'EVI-REM-ANY-TENDENCY-01'),
  ('1a58303f-20db-5c4f-8c35-9762938c4c4a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20404_acts_axes_cash_loads'), 'D', 'admissible only to impeach Stephen, but not as circumstantial proof that he took the receipts.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","offered_for_purpose"]', '["evidence must be conclusive","damaging equals unfairly prejudicial","contradiction evidence is impeachment only"]', 'This choice offers a safe compromise by letting the evidence in only to contradict Stephen. The breaker is that the same cash-gap fact can also be substantive circumstantial proof.', 'The choice uses only to understate the evidence''s substantive purpose.', 'Check whether the same fact also supports the claim substantively.', 'EVI-REM-ANY-TENDENCY-01'),
  ('80b7f87f-9541-5e25-b669-ee1ad5f4db4a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20423_galilee_props_bias'), 'A', 'Overrule the objection because the question targets possible bias from Ruth’s paid tie to the organization that owns Galilee, not her religious beliefs as a truthfulness trait.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only A overrules on the same purpose the stem gives: bias from a paid organizational tie.', NULL, 'REM-EVIDENCE-R610-BIAS-01'),
  ('84964fb1-7bcf-50ce-b050-e39466ebb5be', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20423_galilee_props_bias'), 'B', 'Sustain the objection because any reference to a witness’s religious affiliation is inadmissible.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","offered_for_purpose"]', '["religion_blackout","truthfulness_foundation_overapplied","bias_reputation_only","purpose_ignored"]', 'It turns the Rule 610 objection into a blanket ban, which feels safe because religious references sound prejudicial. The breaker is the offered-purpose split: the question is about a paid organizational tie and bias, not belief-as-truthfulness.', 'The answer overclaims by treating any religious affiliation reference as inadmissible.', 'Circle any and ask whether the purpose is truthfulness or bias.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-R610-BIAS-01'),
  ('a655c3c3-f522-5445-bfca-076a52014a33', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20423_galilee_props_bias'), 'C', 'Overrule the objection only if Ruth’s character for truthfulness has first been attacked.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","offered_for_purpose"]', '["religion_blackout","truthfulness_foundation_overapplied","bias_reputation_only","purpose_ignored"]', 'It borrows the familiar Rule 608(a) sequence, so a student sees truthfulness attacked first and thinks foundation. The breaker is that the offered purpose is bias, not truthful-character rehabilitation.', 'The answer imports a truthfulness-character precondition into a bias-purpose question.', 'Match the answer to the stem’s stated purpose: bias.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-R610-BIAS-01'),
  ('b8fc5aa0-16a2-506e-b632-725a2c7a41e3', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20423_galilee_props_bias'), 'D', 'Sustain the objection because bias may be shown only by reputation evidence.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","offered_for_purpose"]', '["religion_blackout","truthfulness_foundation_overapplied","bias_reputation_only","purpose_ignored"]', 'It confuses bias impeachment with opinion/reputation character proof, which sounds plausible because the bank topic is opinion/reputation. The breaker is that bias is its own credibility purpose and is not limited to reputation evidence.', 'The answer invents a rule that bias may be shown only by reputation evidence.', 'Ask whether the answer created a proof-method limit not in the stem or the Gold Key.', 'REM-EVIDENCE-R610-BIAS-01'),
  ('e64f7c93-c64b-5a0a-b6e3-d860ef9d6a89', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20439_floating_star_driveway'), 'A', 'Lydia was a professional Christmas-pageant director.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["cause_equals_liability","professional_equals_breach","defective_product_equals_any_user_strictly_liable"]', 'The professional title sounds like it carries a higher legal duty. The breaker is that the answer never says Lydia breached any professional or ordinary standard.', 'Professional status does not supply breach.', 'Ask what the professional did unreasonably.', 'REM-TORTS-20439-01'),
  ('d4be717c-566b-5580-bf1c-515f1ab7e4ed', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20439_floating_star_driveway'), 'B', 'Lydia’s conduct was a concurring cause of Timothy’s harm.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["cause_equals_liability","professional_equals_breach","defective_product_equals_any_user_strictly_liable"]', 'Causation sounds like the missing link in a tort case. The breaker is that causation without negligence, intent, or strict liability is only a fragment.', 'Causation alone does not supply a liability basis.', 'Add the question: cause plus what fault or strict-liability category?', 'REM-TORTS-20439-01'),
  ('8d6e628e-59f8-5192-9d44-2d3ac2c18197', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20439_floating_star_driveway'), 'C', 'It was unreasonable for Lydia to test the cable rig in her open driveway beside a public sidewalk.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only C supplies an operative negligence argument: unreasonable conduct under the circumstances.', NULL, 'REM-TORTS-20439-01'),
  ('d15e485b-f9c9-5291-8191-c6b23290b795', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20439_floating_star_driveway'), 'D', 'Lydia is strictly liable for harm resulting from her use of a defective product.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["cause_equals_liability","professional_equals_breach","defective_product_equals_any_user_strictly_liable"]', 'Strict liability and defective-product language sound powerful because they reduce the need to prove fault. The breaker is that Lydia is a user of the rig, not the commercial supplier or distributor.', 'Strict products liability is aimed at commercial sellers or distributors, not a mere user.', 'Use GK-TORTS-USER-SUPPLIER-01.', 'REM-TORTS-20439-01'),
  ('9b3db2c2-748c-5a96-8c1a-af9fa785dfb9', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20461_lydia_beeswax_requirements'), 'A', 'No contract formed unless the court finds $18 per slab was an adequate price.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["requirements contracts are illusory","no fixed quantity means no quantity","courts review adequacy of price","price term means price quote"]', 'A student may think courts must check whether the price was fair before enforcing the deal. The breaker is that price adequacy is not the formation gate.', 'The choice invents a court price-adequacy gate.', 'Ask whether the call is price fairness or quantity sufficiency.', 'RC-CONTRACTS-REQ-QTY-01'),
  ('267642dd-a7a8-58d7-8eb7-34b3bf9e6e87', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20461_lydia_beeswax_requirements'), 'B', 'A contract can form because the quantity is measured by Lydia’s good-faith requirements.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is the only choice that answers the fixed-number objection with the requirements-quantity rule.', NULL, 'RC-CONTRACTS-REQ-QTY-01'),
  ('c2b3f65b-5b49-58fa-a7a9-3da1474220b5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20461_lydia_beeswax_requirements'), 'C', 'No contract formed because the email was only a price quote.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["requirements contracts are illusory","no fixed quantity means no quantity","courts review adequacy of price","price term means price quote"]', 'A student may see a unit price and reach for the price-quote doctrine. The breaker is that the stem gives a buyer''s offer and acceptance, not a seller''s quote.', 'The choice answers a price-quote frame instead of the buyer''s offer and missing-number objection.', 'Read the speaker and verb: Lydia says ''I offer to buy,'' and Barnabas accepted.', 'RC-CONTRACTS-REQ-QTY-01'),
  ('b98ca666-054c-5bff-a476-6a968d975e51', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20461_lydia_beeswax_requirements'), 'D', 'No contract formed because a requirements quantity is always too indefinite and illusory.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["requirements contracts are illusory","no fixed quantity means no quantity","courts review adequacy of price","price term means price quote"]', 'A student may treat no fixed number as no quantity and call the promise illusory. The breaker is the Gold Key that requirements quantity is measured by good-faith needs.', 'The choice says requirements quantity is always too indefinite, which overclaims against the requirements-quantity Gold Key.', 'Mark ''always,'' then apply the requirements-quantity Gold Key.', 'RC-CONTRACTS-REQ-QTY-01'),
  ('c83705db-bc38-58a9-bd24-97c89b24e481', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20476_road_to_bethlehem_sash'), 'A', 'No, because the officer’s continued rolling and rubbing of the tablet through the robe fabric to identify it as contraband exceeded the lawful scope of the frisk; its incriminating character was not immediately apparent.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'A is correct. The frisk began lawfully, but the plain-feel path works only if the contraband character is apparent during the lawful weapons pat-down itself. Here, Hannah knew the object was not a weapon and then rolled and rubbed it through the fabric to figure out what it was. That extra tactile exploration is the defect.

Gold Key: Plain feel requires immediate apparentness. If the officer must manipulate a nonweapon item to identify it as contraband, the frisk has become an additional search.

Silver Key: In the two “No” answers, do not stop at the shared result. Compare the defect each answer names. The winning defect is the extra manipulation before identification, not the mere absence of a warrant after pocket entry.', NULL, 'REM-CRIMINAL-PLAIN-FEEL-01'),
  ('4fdfa299-d079-5b3b-a606-9af02d89b41b', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20476_road_to_bethlehem_sash'), 'B', 'Yes, because the officer had reasonable suspicion that Peter was involved in illegal-pill activity, justifying a search for drugs.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["lawful_stop_means_lawful_search","reasonable_suspicion_for_drugs_authorizes_drug_search","suppression_result_enough_without_correct_reason","terry_frisk_seizes_anything"]', 'The illegal-pill setting makes drug suspicion feel like the central fact. The breaker is that reasonable suspicion answers the wrong question; the call is plain-feel seizure validity.', 'The answer uses drug reasonable suspicion to answer the wrong frame. The call is plain-feel seizure validity.', 'Ask whether the choice answers plain-feel seizure validity.', 'REM-CRIMINAL-PLAIN-FEEL-01'),
  ('fb62f622-6fc3-50e0-8782-40c264a25ddb', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20476_road_to_bethlehem_sash'), 'C', 'No, because the officer needed a warrant before reaching into the sash pocket once she realized the object was not a weapon.', 0, '["wrong_element","wrong_frame"]', '["lawful_stop_means_lawful_search","reasonable_suspicion_for_drugs_authorizes_drug_search","suppression_result_enough_without_correct_reason","terry_frisk_seizes_anything"]', 'The answer gets the suppression outcome and therefore feels safer than the technical answer. The breaker is that it names the wrong defect; the first unlawful move was the manipulation before identification.', 'The answer reaches the right result but names the wrong defect. The defect is manipulation before identification, not simply lack of a warrant before pocket entry.', 'Compare the two No answers by the first unlawful move.', 'REM-CRIMINAL-PLAIN-FEEL-01'),
  ('e719bee2-5146-555e-9ce3-426343cf942d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20476_road_to_bethlehem_sash'), 'D', 'Yes, because the officer was conducting a lawful Terry frisk and any item discovered during the frisk may be seized.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["lawful_stop_means_lawful_search","reasonable_suspicion_for_drugs_authorizes_drug_search","suppression_result_enough_without_correct_reason","terry_frisk_seizes_anything"]', 'The lawful Terry frisk makes the broad permission sound legitimate. The breaker is the absolute ''any item,'' which inflates a limited weapons frisk into a general search.', 'The phrase ''any item'' overstates a lawful Terry frisk. Plain feel does not authorize seizing everything discovered.', 'Mark ''any item'' and apply the plain-feel Gold Key.', 'REM-CRIMINAL-PLAIN-FEEL-01'),
  ('62e8236e-2d16-50f5-a4bf-75f5a5dbf753', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20493_fish_mark_picnic_lot'), 'A', 'Esther, unless the wrapper is later notarized and recorded.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["deed_must_look_official","land_transfer_requires_money","recording_equals_ownership","notary_equals_validity"]', 'The student trusts courthouse ceremony because notarization and recording sound like the official ownership moment. The breaker is that those steps are not the baseline validity condition between the immediate parties.', 'Adds notarization and recording as a validity condition between the parties.', 'Recite the Gold Key and ask whether any third-party priority dispute is in the call.', 'RP-ANCHOR-01'),
  ('1586eb52-8bda-5f0c-a6b1-98698a96ee3f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20493_fish_mark_picnic_lot'), 'B', 'Timothy, because the writing identified the grantor, grantee, land, present transfer, and Esther authenticated it by her mark.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is the only answer that does not add an extra validity gate.', NULL, 'RP-ANCHOR-01'),
  ('97c2d76e-f56f-5deb-8644-f67d9be3d321', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20493_fish_mark_picnic_lot'), 'C', 'Esther, because a deed must be prepared on a formal real-estate deed form.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["deed_must_look_official","land_transfer_requires_money","recording_equals_ownership","notary_equals_validity"]', 'The student judges the wrapper by appearance and assumes land transfers need official-looking paper. The breaker is that the tested rule requires a sufficient writing, not a formal printed deed form.', 'Adds a formal printed deed form as a validity condition.', 'Inventory writing, parties, land, present transfer, authentication, delivery, and acceptance.', 'RP-ANCHOR-01'),
  ('3fbdddb5-9fa2-5ad1-b227-57c8430d712f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20493_fish_mark_picnic_lot'), 'D', 'Esther, because Timothy paid no consideration.', 0, '["fabricated_rule","wrong_frame"]', '["deed_must_look_official","land_transfer_requires_money","recording_equals_ownership","notary_equals_validity"]', 'The student imports contract consideration and treats the transfer as defective because no money changed hands. The breaker is that an otherwise valid delivered deed can make a gratuitous conveyance.', 'Adds consideration as a validity condition for a delivered deed.', 'Say: a deed can be a gift if the transfer formalities are met.', 'RP-ANCHOR-01'),
  ('43c1e74e-4954-5bae-8768-34b64e531b4c', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20496_loaves_prop_cart'), 'A', 'Denied, because the payment from Lydia''s insurer was not made after any court decided that Daniel was liable.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["double_recovery_always_barred","insurance_payments_always_reduce_damages","partial_indemnity_applies_to_insurers"]', 'The student sees the right result, denial, and accepts the first plausible reason attached to it. The breaker is that judicial determination is not the source-identity switch.', 'The choice gives the right outcome but rests on judicial determination, not payment source.', 'Ask: court determination or payment source?', 'TOR-REM-COLLATERAL-SOURCE-01'),
  ('d2f7db1d-dd10-5dda-9405-6b8b81cf55e8', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20496_loaves_prop_cart'), 'B', 'Granted, because Daniel is entitled to partial indemnity.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["double_recovery_always_barred","insurance_payments_always_reduce_damages","partial_indemnity_applies_to_insurers"]', 'The student recognizes partial indemnity as a serious tort-allocation phrase. The breaker is that indemnity belongs to common-liability actors, not plaintiff-side insurance.', 'The choice imports partial indemnity from the joint-tortfeasor allocation frame.', 'Reserve indemnity/contribution for common-liability actors.', 'TOR-REM-COLLATERAL-SOURCE-01'),
  ('c745cda0-ea29-5d8b-bab3-f1a0f58dbc82', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20496_loaves_prop_cart'), 'C', 'Denied, because Lydia''s insurer was not acting for anyone who was liable to Lydia for negligence.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only C is true and responsive after applying the Gold Key.', NULL, 'TOR-REM-COLLATERAL-SOURCE-01'),
  ('23ede970-f2c5-52d3-a27b-0ae00215de62', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20496_loaves_prop_cart'), 'D', 'Granted, because Lydia should not be allowed to recover twice for the same medical expenses.', 0, '["colloquialism"]', '["double_recovery_always_barred","insurance_payments_always_reduce_damages","partial_indemnity_applies_to_insurers"]', 'The student wants to prevent a double recovery and follows common-sense fairness. The breaker is the collateral-source Gold Key: plaintiff-side insurance does not reduce the tortfeasor''s judgment.', 'The choice uses double-recovery fairness language that the collateral-source rule defeats.', 'Plaintiff-side insurance is collateral.', 'TOR-REM-COLLATERAL-SOURCE-01'),
  ('712f585c-8af7-5eb2-9ae6-9790c194c38e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20516_manna_games_duress'), 'A', 'Yes, because the threat was directed at Timothy’s sister, a close family member, which is sufficient.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["family threat is automatically sufficient","reasonable fear is automatically sufficient","duress is only for violent crimes"]', 'The student sees a close-family threat and recognizes a real duress element. The breaker is that one real element does not answer the threshold failure: no imminent threat.', 'The choice names the close-family fact but does not answer the missing imminence threshold.', 'Ask whether the answer also proves imminence and no reasonable legal alternative.', 'REM-CRIM-DURESS-IMMINENCE'),
  ('0dcf8f76-c74a-5ab7-a2c7-d14827de407f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20516_manna_games_duress'), 'B', 'No, because the threat was not imminent — the threatened harm was scheduled for a future time and Barnabas was physically absent.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct.

Gold Key: Common-law duress is not a “real fear” defense. It needs an imminent human threat of death or serious bodily harm, directed at the defendant or a close family member, with no reasonable legal alternative. Here, the threat was for a future time, and Barnabas was physically absent. Timothy had time to seek help or protect Hannah without stealing.

Silver Key: Read the answer array as an element-completion test. Two “Yes” answers name sympathetic facts. The credited “No” answer names the missing threshold.', NULL, 'REM-CRIM-DURESS-IMMINENCE'),
  ('3a45de66-fde7-5f9e-83f3-1690e5141dbc', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20516_manna_games_duress'), 'C', 'No, because duress is available only as a defense to violent crimes.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["family threat is automatically sufficient","reasonable fear is automatically sufficient","duress is only for violent crimes"]', 'The student reaches a no-defense result and remembers that duress has crime-scope limits. The breaker is that the limit is not a violent-crime-only rule; theft is not excluded if the other elements are met.', 'The choice uses an absolute violent-crime-only rule that is not the duress scope rule.', 'Treat ''only'' as a red flag and recall that theft is not excluded from duress.', 'REM-CRIM-DURESS-IMMINENCE'),
  ('a9ae2479-072d-559a-a928-b52c8b5e6d1d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20516_manna_games_duress'), 'D', 'Yes, because Timothy had a genuine and reasonable fear that Barnabas would hurt Hannah.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["family threat is automatically sufficient","reasonable fear is automatically sufficient","duress is only for violent crimes"]', 'The student credits Timothy''s fear because the stem makes it believable and reasonable. The breaker is that genuine fear still does not supply immediacy or eliminate legal alternatives.', 'The choice proves fear but not imminence or lack of reasonable legal alternative.', 'Separate believable fear from immediate compulsion.', 'REM-CRIM-DURESS-IMMINENCE'),
  ('899f64cf-ebdf-50a4-a594-da32ccd91739', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20523_easter_stage_guaranty'), 'A', 'No, because a guaranty memorandum must always be signed by both Peter and Ruth.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["memo_must_go_to_creditor","debtor_must_sign_guaranty","both_parties_must_sign","recipient_controls_sof","formalism_over_content"]', 'It feels safer because a guaranty involves both the debtor and the guarantor. The breaker is that the suit charges Ruth, so Peter’s signature is an added formality.', 'The choice adds an always-both-sign requirement. The Gold Key cuts the extra signature condition.', 'Ask whose promise the supplier is enforcing.', 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-SOF-MEMO-ADDRESSEE-01'),
  ('c72fd2ac-5703-5418-be9f-c0810b5ca20e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20523_easter_stage_guaranty'), 'B', 'Yes, because a signed memorandum by Ruth, the party to be charged, can satisfy the writing requirement even when sent to someone other than the supplier, if it sufficiently identifies the promise and parties.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. Ruth is the person being sued on the suretyship promise. The note is signed by Ruth, identifies the supplier, identifies Peter’s debt, states the amount, and states Ruth’s promise to cover the debt if Peter fails to pay. Gold Key: for a common-law Statute of Frauds memorandum, the key question is whether the writing is signed by the party to be charged and sufficiently identifies the promise and parties; it need not be addressed to the enforcing creditor. Silver Key: three choices add extra formalities; the answer array is asking whether the addressee and extra signatures are required.', NULL, 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-SOF-MEMO-ADDRESSEE-01'),
  ('9b8d5466-3704-579e-b4e7-7510cb2e9cbc', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20523_easter_stage_guaranty'), 'C', 'No, because a suretyship memorandum must be sent or addressed to the creditor seeking to enforce it.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["memo_must_go_to_creditor","debtor_must_sign_guaranty","both_parties_must_sign","recipient_controls_sof","formalism_over_content"]', 'It mirrors Ruth’s stated objection that the note went to Lydia instead of the supplier. The breaker is that addressee identity is not the memorandum-sufficiency test.', 'The choice makes addressee identity decisive. The Gold Key cuts the creditor-addressee requirement.', 'Apply the Gold Key: signer and content, not addressee.', 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-SOF-MEMO-ADDRESSEE-01'),
  ('0e07ce4c-f4ef-5ae4-8819-d0881ed7544a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20523_easter_stage_guaranty'), 'D', 'Yes, but only if Peter also signed Ruth’s note.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["memo_must_go_to_creditor","debtor_must_sign_guaranty","both_parties_must_sign","recipient_controls_sof","formalism_over_content"]', 'It sounds like a careful yes answer because it adds Peter’s signature as a safeguard. The breaker is that Peter is not the party being charged on Ruth’s promise.', 'The choice adds Peter’s signature as a condition. The Gold Key cuts the debtor-signature requirement.', 'Peter’s signature is not required to charge Ruth.', 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-SOF-MEMO-ADDRESSEE-01'),
  ('0932a1d1-c257-5879-aec8-c56d4f5c8ce2', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20542_praise_festival_cashbox'), 'A', 'No, because Peter was not in custody when the detectives spoke with him.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["custody_required","different_label_controls","indictment_bars_all_questioning","same_event_not_enough_without_same_offense_check"]', 'A student sees a police-questioning problem and reaches for custody because custody is a real Miranda trigger. The breaker is that the call is Sixth Amendment deliberate elicitation after attachment, not Fifth Amendment custodial interrogation.', 'The choice uses a Fifth Amendment custody frame when the call asks for Sixth Amendment suppression after attachment.', 'Mark custody as wrong-frame unless the call asks Fifth Amendment or Miranda.', 'CRIM-REM-20542-SAME-OFFENSE'),
  ('8fb0c67a-bad2-5298-b7b6-01f6c02c951c', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20542_praise_festival_cashbox'), 'B', 'Yes, because the questioning concerned the same charged criminal episode and a same-offense variant after attachment.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. Peter had been indicted and counsel had been appointed. The detectives then deliberately sought an admission about the same festival-booth incident, merely recast as an unarmed theft rather than armed robbery. They did this without counsel and without a waiver. Gold Key: after attachment, the Sixth Amendment bars deliberate elicitation about the charged offense, and a lesser-included or same-offense relabeling does not create a clean new offense. Silver Key: do not let the answer turn on the noun-label; lock the call to “Sixth Amendment after indictment” and ask whether the new question is really about the charged event.', NULL, 'CRIM-REM-20542-SAME-OFFENSE'),
  ('334e0691-8dfa-5501-86ff-69f486bf0f44', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20542_praise_festival_cashbox'), 'C', 'Yes, because police may not question an indicted defendant about any unrelated offense.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["custody_required","different_label_controls","indictment_bars_all_questioning","same_event_not_enough_without_same_offense_check"]', 'A student remembers that indictment gives the defendant a strong counsel right and inflates it into a universal shield. The breaker is that the Sixth Amendment right is offense-specific, so unrelated-crime questioning is not categorically barred by this rule.', 'The choice overclaims by treating indictment as a bar to questioning about any unrelated offense.', 'Strike any answer that bars any unrelated offense unless a Gold Key says the right is global.', 'CRIM-REM-20542-SAME-OFFENSE'),
  ('4ad953d6-f2af-5a50-9df6-433e0d068c61', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20542_praise_festival_cashbox'), 'D', 'No, because unarmed theft and armed robbery use different labels.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["custody_required","different_label_controls","indictment_bars_all_questioning","same_event_not_enough_without_same_offense_check"]', 'A student remembers the true phrase offense-specific and treats different crime names as enough. The breaker is that the stem points to the same charged event in a lesser-offense costume, so label-only reasoning is not responsive.', 'The choice borrows offense-specificity but answers by formal labels rather than same-offense substance.', 'Compare the event and lesser-included relation before trusting labels.', 'CRIM-REM-20542-SAME-OFFENSE'),
  ('5111dd39-6760-56f2-b63a-fbb600e00143', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20546_jericho_wall_studio'), 'A', 'Mary had paid the workshop fee before the panel struck her.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["causation alone is enough","contractor fault controls owner liability","purchase required for invitee status","defective product automatically creates liability against premises owner"]', 'The payment fact feels useful because business transactions often mark who counts as a protected customer. The breaker is that the claim needs owner-linked inspection or repair, not a completed payment.', 'The payment fact addresses entrant/status flavor but does not supply Lydia''s inspection breach.', 'Ask whether the choice proves Lydia knew, should have known, inspected, or failed to fix.', 'REM-TORTS-NAMED-DEFENDANT-INSPECTION-01'),
  ('d6fb39c4-b29e-5dd6-9994-481c7fe21658', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20546_jericho_wall_studio'), 'B', 'A reasonable inspection by Lydia would have disclosed that the panel swung into the aisle improperly.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is the best answer. It connects the injury to Lydia’s own premises duty. The claim is against Lydia, not Barnabas and not the manufacturer. The added fact says a reasonable inspection by Lydia would have revealed the improper swing before Mary was injured. That supplies the owner-side breach path the call is asking for.

Gold Key: For a business invitee, the owner’s live duty is reasonable inspection and protection against dangerous conditions the owner knows about or would discover by reasonable care. Silver Key: Lock the named defendant first. The answer must create liability for Lydia, not merely explain how the device failed, whether Barnabas was careful, or whether Mary paid.', NULL, 'REM-TORTS-NAMED-DEFENDANT-INSPECTION-01'),
  ('93296981-a074-5250-90a8-143d22e1f476', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20546_jericho_wall_studio'), 'C', 'Mary’s injury resulted from a defect in the pressure mat.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["causation alone is enough","contractor fault controls owner liability","purchase required for invitee status","defective product automatically creates liability against premises owner"]', 'The defect fact feels powerful because a broken device sounds like the cause of the injury. The breaker is that it points to product or manufacturer responsibility, not Lydia''s discoverable premises breach.', 'The product-defect fact points to the product chain unless tied to Lydia''s discoverable premises condition.', 'Ask whether the defendant sold the product or whether the defect was discoverable by owner inspection.', 'REM-TORTS-NAMED-DEFENDANT-INSPECTION-01'),
  ('e09bc692-b103-5691-b11f-b942aa244017', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20546_jericho_wall_studio'), 'D', 'Barnabas was not negligent in installing the Jericho Wall display.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["causation alone is enough","contractor fault controls owner liability","purchase required for invitee status","defective product automatically creates liability against premises owner"]', 'The no-negligence fact feels helpful because it removes blame from Barnabas. The breaker is that removing another actor''s fault does not supply Lydia''s inspection breach.', 'Barnabas''s lack of negligence does not prove Lydia''s negligence.', 'Cross out third-party fault facts unless they supply owner breach.', 'REM-TORTS-NAMED-DEFENDANT-INSPECTION-01'),
  ('c157773c-d455-59de-b81b-aa888031126e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20556_mustard_seed_puppet_caravan'), 'A', 'Stephen, since he never personally notified Martha that he would not report for the caravan job.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["performance_date_controls_everything","direct_notice_required","legal_label_beats_fact","later_cure_revives_contract"]', 'The student sees that Stephen never personally said he would miss the job and treats direct notice as decisive. The breaker is that Martha already had reasonable knowledge and changed position before Stephen became available again.', 'This choice answers personal notice, but the call turns on reasonable knowledge and reliance before cure.', 'Ask what Martha knew and whether she changed position before Stephen''s release.', 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-PI-01'),
  ('f3b1dffb-7d45-52f3-bcf7-de54f2a91703', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20556_mustard_seed_puppet_caravan'), 'B', 'Martha, since Stephen''s contract with the overseas tour was an anticipatory repudiation of his contract with Martha.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["performance_date_controls_everything","direct_notice_required","legal_label_beats_fact","later_cure_revives_contract"]', 'The student recognizes future nonperformance vocabulary and grabs the most familiar label. The breaker is that the credited answer must state the reliance-before-cure fact, not merely a label.', 'This choice gives a nearby legal label but omits the reliance-before-cure fact that resolves the item.', 'Use the Silver Key: label-only loses to reliance/timing.', 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-PI-01'),
  ('ccc21ef4-5421-57bd-a36b-efa70c87fbbe', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20556_mustard_seed_puppet_caravan'), 'C', 'Martha, since Martha hired Barnabas in reliance on the reasonable belief that Stephen would be unable to perform as agreed.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is the only answer that states both the defendant-side outcome and the reliance/timing fact that resolves the later cure.', NULL, 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-PI-01'),
  ('d0852e9e-599a-552e-9f82-29fc5ee011d9', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20556_mustard_seed_puppet_caravan'), 'D', 'Stephen, since he was ready, willing, and able to perform as agreed on January 10.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["performance_date_controls_everything","direct_notice_required","legal_label_beats_fact","later_cure_revives_contract"]', 'The student focuses on the clean plaintiff fact that Stephen appeared ready on the day performance was due. The breaker is that Martha''s replacement contract came before Stephen''s release from the outside tour.', 'This choice uses the later performance-date fact, but the trigger fact is earlier reliance.', 'Mark reliance before cure.', 'CONTRACTS-ANCHOR-PI-01'),
  ('6493a75a-b8fe-5ce1-bc55-eabf588b5b72', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20565_purple_gear_hymnbook_tote'), 'A', 'Admit the gear because the manufacturer can argue about its weight.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["jury_decides_everything","weight_not_admissibility_overused","opponent_must_disprove","physical_object_auto_admit"]', 'The choice sells the common instinct that flaws go only to weight once the item is in the courtroom. The breaker is the missing foundation gate; without a threshold link, the jury never reaches weight.', 'A answers the later weight question before the foundation gate is crossed.', 'Ask whether there is any foundation link before discussing weight.', 'RM-EVI-FOUNDATION-GATE-01'),
  ('2d941198-6a8c-58df-bda0-f346182915e4', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20565_purple_gear_hymnbook_tote'), 'B', 'Exclude the gear because there is no evidence sufficient to support a finding that it is connected to the fog machine or the accident.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. The gear is offered as if it is connected to the fog machine or the pageant accident, but the stem gives no identifying witness, no recognizable marking, and no circumstance tying the gear to that product or event. Gold Key: A physical object needs a threshold link before the jury can consider it as case evidence. Silver Key: Gate before weight; the jury does not weigh an object that has not crossed the foundation gate.', NULL, 'RM-EVI-FOUNDATION-GATE-01'),
  ('37aa8015-8d6d-5f22-a8f9-2129596fbf3a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20565_purple_gear_hymnbook_tote'), 'C', 'Exclude the gear only if the manufacturer proves it came from some other device.', 0, '["backwards"]', '["jury_decides_everything","weight_not_admissibility_overused","opponent_must_disprove","physical_object_auto_admit"]', 'The choice sells a burden-shift story: exclude only after the opponent proves a different source. The breaker is the proponent''s first move; the offering party must supply the link.', 'C reverses the first-showing burden by requiring the opponent to prove another source.', 'Ask who is offering the item and who must supply the first link.', 'RM-EVI-FOUNDATION-GATE-01'),
  ('c3cfeed7-4b60-5c7d-a4b0-6af17953ad1a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20565_purple_gear_hymnbook_tote'), 'D', 'Admit the gear because any physical object may be considered by the jury.', 0, '["tiered_absolute"]', '["jury_decides_everything","weight_not_admissibility_overused","opponent_must_disprove","physical_object_auto_admit"]', 'The choice sells trust-the-jury breadth and makes all physical things sound eligible. The breaker is the word any; the rule still requires a case connection.', 'D overclaims by saying any physical object may be considered by the jury.', 'Mark ''any'' and check whether the rule really has no gate.', 'RM-EVI-FOUNDATION-GATE-01'),
  ('99da1dd1-51d0-5501-952e-3383c20df6e5', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20567_psalm_panels_venue'), 'A', 'Whichever rule would require dismissal, because Erie discourages forum shopping.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["Erie always means state law","forum shopping beats federal statute","diversity cases lack federal venue rules"]', 'The student remembers that Erie worries about forum shopping and treats that worry as the whole test. The breaker is that Erie policy does not override a valid federal statute directly on point.', 'Forum-shopping concerns are real Erie bait, but the answer skips the federal-statute-on-point step.', 'Run the Gold Key before Erie balancing.', 'CIV-REM-ERIE-FED-STATUTE-01'),
  ('d37c9484-e6c0-5b30-b47b-e26e1bff3215', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20567_psalm_panels_venue'), 'B', 'Neither rule, because a diversity case in federal court has no venue requirement.', 0, '["contradiction"]', '["Erie always means state law","forum shopping beats federal statute","diversity cases lack federal venue rules"]', 'The student may confuse diversity jurisdiction with a free pass from procedural venue analysis. The breaker is that the stem itself gives venue statutes, so the no-venue answer fights the setup.', 'The answer denies venue requirements even though the stem names venue statutes.', 'Cut answers that contradict the setup.', 'CIV-REM-ERIE-FED-STATUTE-01'),
  ('3f49c1d0-bae4-53d2-bf76-ac1a20647adb', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20567_psalm_panels_venue'), 'C', 'Section 1391, because a valid federal statute directly controls federal venue.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. The call asks which venue rule the federal court should apply. The stem supplies a federal venue statute that directly governs venue in a federal district where a substantial part of the events occurred. The events occurred in the chosen federal district.

Gold Key: When a valid federal statute directly controls a federal-court procedural issue, apply the federal statute before doing Erie twin-aims balancing.

Silver Key: Lock the call as a rule-source question, not a dismissal-outcome question. The answer is the rule that controls federal venue, not the rule that makes one party win fastest.', NULL, 'CIV-REM-ERIE-FED-STATUTE-01'),
  ('954e1a8a-ffca-5931-be52-69054b8959fe', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20567_psalm_panels_venue'), 'D', 'The state county venue statute, because Mary’s claim arises under state law.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["Erie always means state law","forum shopping beats federal statute","diversity cases lack federal venue rules"]', 'The student hears state-law claim and jumps to state law controls. The breaker is that venue in federal court is directly governed by the federal statute named in the stem.', 'The answer uses state-law-claim language to answer the wrong layer.', 'Ask whether the procedural issue is directly governed by a federal statute.', 'CIV-REM-ERIE-FED-STATUTE-01'),
  ('ed58e256-f358-5e68-a2ad-79e28a5355a3', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20569_ark_float'), 'A', 'Lydia breached unless the city engineer’s order made use of the float impossible.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["initial_effectiveness_means_permanent_duty","impossibility_required_for_discharge","substantial_performance_overrides_condition"]', 'The student reaches for impossibility because it sounds like a familiar excuse doctrine. The breaker is that the contract already named a different terminating event.', 'This choice replaces the contract''s below-threshold order trigger with impossibility.', 'Ask: what event did the contract itself say would end the rental?', 'RM-CONTRACTS-CONDITION-SUBSEQUENT-01'),
  ('5a7342cb-fca2-5dac-8db3-60fb1b8dc3ef', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20569_ark_float'), 'B', 'Lydia’s duty to provide the float was discharged by the condition subsequent stated in the rental agreement.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is the only choice that uses the exact trigger and the effect of that trigger.', NULL, 'RM-CONTRACTS-CONDITION-SUBSEQUENT-01'),
  ('6fcb4ca6-f25f-5fea-a274-3688dcfe179a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20569_ark_float'), 'C', 'Ruth may compel delivery of the float because substantial performance of the parade plan is enough.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["initial_effectiveness_means_permanent_duty","impossibility_required_for_discharge","substantial_performance_overrides_condition"]', 'The student reaches for substantial performance because it sounds like a forgiving contracts rule. The breaker is that Ruth''s performance plan does not decide Lydia''s duty after the stated condition occurred.', 'This choice replaces the duty-discharge question with substantial performance of the parade plan.', 'Return to Lydia''s duty to provide the float after the order.', 'RM-CONTRACTS-CONDITION-SUBSEQUENT-01'),
  ('9253d50a-e88a-558f-ba9f-b8ded62fb13e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20569_ark_float'), 'D', 'Lydia breached because the float rental was already effective when signed.', 0, '["wrong_element"]', '["initial_effectiveness_means_permanent_duty","impossibility_required_for_discharge","substantial_performance_overrides_condition"]', 'The student sees that the rental was effective at signing and treats that as enough. The breaker is that the later ''unless'' event is the dispositive fact.', 'This choice answers whether the rental was initially effective, not what happened after the later trigger.', 'Continue from signing to the later city-engineer order.', 'RM-CONTRACTS-CONDITION-SUBSEQUENT-01'),
  ('e01504c5-6e2c-5555-9020-da3b0a36811b', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20586_psalms_hormone_use'), 'A', 'Whether the statute is medically unwise, because bad medical policy automatically triggers strict scrutiny.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["bad_policy_equals_strict_scrutiny","same_medication_equals_sex_classification","minors_equal_adults_everywhere"]', 'A student may think a medically disputed rule must be constitutionally suspicious. The breaker is that bad policy does not automatically trigger strict scrutiny.', 'The answer says bad medical policy automatically triggers strict scrutiny. The automatic trigger is the visible overclaim.', 'Circle automatically and ask whether policy wisdom is a suspect classification.', 'REM-CONLAW-CLASSIFICATION-FIRST-20586'),
  ('dd25d8ca-c124-5b91-b046-5dcd8166d3e7', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20586_psalms_hormone_use'), 'B', 'Whether minors must be treated the same as adults in every medical setting.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["bad_policy_equals_strict_scrutiny","same_medication_equals_sex_classification","minors_equal_adults_everywhere"]', 'A student may see the adult/minor contrast and jump to minors'' rights. The breaker is that the answer says every medical setting and misses the classification threshold.', 'The answer says minors must be treated like adults in every medical setting. The every-setting language is visibly overbroad.', 'Return to the question: the threshold is the classification drawn, not every adult/minor medical right.', 'REM-CONLAW-CLASSIFICATION-FIRST-20586'),
  ('2d7e415b-4831-525a-a521-8dc418f2ec57', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20586_psalms_hormone_use'), 'C', 'Whether the statute classifies by medical use and age, rather than by sex as such.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. Silver Key: On an Equal Protection threshold call, do not start with whether the policy is good or bad. Start with the line the law actually draws. Gold Key: A medical-use-and-age line does not become a sex classification merely because the same medication is allowed for other diagnoses; the threshold question is what classification the statute itself draws.

The answer tracks the threshold task: classify the statute before choosing a scrutiny tier.', NULL, 'REM-CONLAW-CLASSIFICATION-FIRST-20586'),
  ('da3297b5-6cdf-5f34-b47c-fe507bb51850', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20586_psalms_hormone_use'), 'D', 'Whether the hormone medication is prescribed for other diagnoses, because that fact alone automatically proves sex discrimination.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","wrong_frame"]', '["bad_policy_equals_strict_scrutiny","same_medication_equals_sex_classification","minors_equal_adults_everywhere"]', 'A student may treat same medication for other diagnoses as enough to prove discrimination. The breaker is that fact alone does not automatically prove sex classification.', 'The answer says same medication elsewhere fact alone automatically proves sex discrimination. The Gold Key confirms why that automatic inference fails.', 'Separate medical use from sex-as-such classification.', 'REM-CONLAW-CLASSIFICATION-FIRST-20586'),
  ('a5810e0e-5dbe-5875-bb4f-17e85a391ef0', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20594_daniels_whale_float'), 'A', 'Lydia, because a rescuer is entitled to indemnity from the person whom the rescuer was attempting to rescue.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","violation_vs_remedy"]', '["rescuers_always_get_indemnity","no_actual_awareness_no_duty","rescuer_as_officious_intermeddler"]', 'The choice rewards the instinct that rescuers deserve reimbursement. The breaker is that rescue doctrine is not automatic indemnity; it requires negligent danger and foreseeable rescue.', 'Automatic rescuer indemnity overclaims the legal basis for recovery.', 'Ask whether the answer states negligence-based recovery or a blanket remedy.', 'REM-TORTS-RESCUE-20594'),
  ('4b5d4435-7b78-539c-994a-0e97c9b0232d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20594_daniels_whale_float'), 'B', 'Daniel, because Daniel did not know that Lydia would try to rescue him.', 0, '["wrong_element","wrong_frame"]', '["rescuers_always_get_indemnity","no_actual_awareness_no_duty","rescuer_as_officious_intermeddler"]', 'The choice makes Daniel''s lack of actual knowledge feel decisive. The breaker is that the rescue rule uses foreseeability of rescue, not actual awareness of this rescuer.', 'Actual awareness is not the dispositive element; foreseeable rescue is.', 'Use the Gold Key: rescue is foreseeable when danger invites it.', 'REM-TORTS-RESCUE-20594'),
  ('376f57b1-5b33-5147-a084-5cdbb5ad8a5f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20594_daniels_whale_float'), 'C', 'Lydia, because her injury resulted from Daniel’s failure to act reasonably.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'C is correct. Gold Key: Danger invites rescue. When Daniel unreasonably created a danger to human life, including his own, a rescue attempt was a foreseeable response. Lydia’s injury came from trying to respond to that danger, so the negligence answer that ties her injury to Daniel’s unreasonable conduct is the credited answer.

Silver Key: On a “because” answer set, do not pick the party first. Test the because-clause. C wins because it gives the legally operative ground: unreasonable danger causing a foreseeable rescue injury.', NULL, 'REM-TORTS-RESCUE-20594'),
  ('80405a53-fc62-53d4-aba2-c80dec2ce01e', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20594_daniels_whale_float'), 'D', 'Daniel, because Lydia was an officious intermeddler.', 0, '["misfit","wrong_frame"]', '["rescuers_always_get_indemnity","no_actual_awareness_no_duty","rescuer_as_officious_intermeddler"]', 'The choice uses a formal-sounding label that makes Lydia look like a meddler. The breaker is that apparent human peril gives her a legitimate rescue reason.', 'The officious-intermeddler frame does not fit an apparent human rescue.', 'Check whether the plaintiff had a legitimate rescue reason.', 'REM-TORTS-RESCUE-20594'),
  ('5fe175b8-ce8c-5840-b6cf-b8cead0f6db1', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20597_olivewood_nativity_craft_swap'), 'A', 'Both Stephen and Mary are not guilty because both acted from genuine beliefs that excused the taking.', 0, '["extreme_of_range"]', '["all_mistakes_require_reasonableness","sincerity_excuses_law_mistake","careless_fact_mistake_cannot_help"]', 'A student picks this because both actors are described as genuine or sincere. The breaker is that sincerity does not erase the fact/law distinction.', 'This extends the excuse from fact mistake to law mistake.', 'Ask what each defendant was mistaken about before judging guilt.', 'CRIM-REM-MISTAKE-FACT-LAW-01'),
  ('c45ad545-4953-5891-8cb7-824301028daf', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20597_olivewood_nativity_craft_swap'), 'B', 'Both Stephen and Mary are guilty because only reasonable mistakes can provide a defense.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["all_mistakes_require_reasonableness","sincerity_excuses_law_mistake","careless_fact_mistake_cannot_help"]', 'A student picks this because reasonableness sounds like a familiar mistake-defense requirement. The breaker is that the stem says specific intent, so Stephen''s honest fact mistake need not be reasonable.', 'This imports a reasonableness requirement from the wrong mistake-defense frame.', 'When the stem says specific intent, test whether the fact mistake negates that intent.', 'CRIM-REM-MISTAKE-FACT-LAW-01'),
  ('f258018a-7ceb-5481-b81f-8c31a44dac1a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20597_olivewood_nativity_craft_swap'), 'C', 'Stephen is not guilty because his honest mistake of fact negates the specific intent for larceny; Mary is guilty because mistake of law is generally no defense.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'It is true and responsive to both scenarios.', NULL, 'CRIM-REM-MISTAKE-FACT-LAW-01'),
  ('cc7f457b-f40d-5c69-9b86-22a764615246', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20597_olivewood_nativity_craft_swap'), 'D', 'Stephen is guilty; Mary is not guilty—his mistake was unreasonable, and her mistake concerned the law and is a valid defense.', 0, '["backwards"]', '["all_mistakes_require_reasonableness","sincerity_excuses_law_mistake","careless_fact_mistake_cannot_help"]', 'A student picks this because Stephen''s assumption feels careless and Mary''s legal belief sounds principled. The breaker is direction: fact mistake can help Stephen, while law mistake generally does not help Mary.', 'This reverses both outcomes.', 'State the direction aloud: fact mistake helps; law mistake usually does not.', 'CRIM-REM-MISTAKE-FACT-LAW-01'),
  ('2258bb77-5949-5a15-8187-251f47909c36', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20598_write_it_on_your_heart'), 'A', 'No, because the ad portrayed the guide character in a respectful and admiring way.', 0, '["colloquialism"]', '["appropriation_requires_name_or_photo","flattery_defeats_privacy_claim","appropriation_requires_false_fact"]', 'A student picks this because flattering use feels harmless. The breaker is that the call turns on unauthorized commercial identity use, not insult.', 'Respectful tone feels harmless, but the call asks commercial identity use.', 'Ask whether the answer uses a legal trigger or only a tone judgment.', 'REM-TORTS-APPROPRIATION-IDENTITY-01'),
  ('4e1841b9-5d9e-57c7-9007-0191bc843eac', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20598_write_it_on_your_heart'), 'B', 'Yes, because the company used Ruth’s distinctive identity for commercial advantage without consent.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'Only B is both true and responsive to the appropriation call.', NULL, 'REM-TORTS-APPROPRIATION-IDENTITY-01'),
  ('7beb6ec3-6a10-5dac-8417-5841753a583a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20598_write_it_on_your_heart'), 'C', 'Yes, but only if the ad stated a false fact about Ruth.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["appropriation_requires_name_or_photo","flattery_defeats_privacy_claim","appropriation_requires_false_fact"]', 'A student picks this because false statements feel like the familiar reputation-tort path. The breaker is that this is an identity-use call, and the Gold Key makes false-fact language a neighbor-frame trap.', 'False fact is a neighbor-frame answer, not the appropriation call.', 'Name the call: appropriation. Then remove false-statement conditions unless the call asks for a reputation tort.', 'REM-TORTS-APPROPRIATION-IDENTITY-01'),
  ('8ac8ed37-b75c-549e-a3ec-62b10d1e25a9', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20598_write_it_on_your_heart'), 'D', 'No, because the ad did not use Ruth’s exact name or photograph.', 0, '["fabricated_rule"]', '["appropriation_requires_name_or_photo","flattery_defeats_privacy_claim","appropriation_requires_false_fact"]', 'A student picks this because exact name or photo feels like the safest proof of identity use. The breaker is that the Gold Key says recognizable commercial evocation can be enough.', 'Exact name/photo is an added requirement defeated by the Gold Key.', 'Use the identity-evocation Gold Key: recognizable commercial imitation can be enough.', 'REM-TORTS-APPROPRIATION-IDENTITY-01'),
  ('6631a783-c6eb-54cb-a806-9ad00ecbec7f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20599_advent_handbell_integration'), 'A', 'Exclude the oral promise because the writing was intended as a complete and exclusive statement of the parties’ agreement.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'The complete-and-exclusive phrase defeats the prior oral consistent add-on.', NULL, 'REM-CONTRACTS-COMPLETE-INTEGRATION-01'),
  ('f4fda2d5-e44f-5872-9dc8-996cd0fde22d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20599_advent_handbell_integration'), 'B', 'Admit the oral promise because it does not conflict with any term in the signed writing.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","wrong_frame"]', '["noncontradiction_is_enough","merger_clauses_are_goods_only","omitted_term_voids_writing"]', 'The student sees no direct conflict and treats consistency as enough. The breaker is the complete-and-exclusive signal, which moves the question from contradiction to integration level.', 'It uses the partial-integration consistency frame when the stem gives a complete-and-exclusive writing.', 'Circle complete and exclusive before evaluating consistency.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-COMPLETE-INTEGRATION-01'),
  ('3fd7a21a-e981-55aa-aa97-b1e7464fd46d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20599_advent_handbell_integration'), 'C', 'Exclude the signed writing because it left out the handbell cue sheet.', 0, '["misfit"]', '["noncontradiction_is_enough","merger_clauses_are_goods_only","omitted_term_voids_writing"]', 'The student thinks an omitted promised feature damages the signed document. The breaker is that the offered evidence is the oral promise, not the signed writing.', 'It excludes the signed writing even though the offered evidence is the oral promise.', 'Ask what evidence the proponent is offering.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-COMPLETE-INTEGRATION-01'),
  ('9334448d-aea3-5012-96f9-3cb897c996ae', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20599_advent_handbell_integration'), 'D', 'Admit the oral promise because merger clauses affect only sales of goods.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","wrong_frame"]', '["noncontradiction_is_enough","merger_clauses_are_goods_only","omitted_term_voids_writing"]', 'The student recognizes UCC parol-evidence language and assumes merger clauses live only there. The breaker is the Gold Key: complete integration is also a common-law services-contract concept.', 'It falsely limits merger clauses to sales of goods.', 'Use the Gold Key: complete integration is not goods-only.', 'REM-CONTRACTS-COMPLETE-INTEGRATION-01'),
  ('5743e5d6-6b09-5a72-8946-d68735bca32a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20602_davids_harp_projector'), 'A', 'Admit the evidence because the hinge change is relevant and relevant evidence is generally admissible.', 0, '["bait_doctrine","offered_for_purpose"]', '["negligence_only_rule407","relevance_is_enough","feasibility_magic_word","automatic_exception"]', 'The student remembers that relevant evidence usually comes in. The breaker is that Rule 407 is a specific public-policy exclusion and the answer never handles the offered purpose.', 'General relevance is true as a background idea but does not answer the specific Rule 407 public-policy exclusion.', 'Ask whether the answer addresses the named exclusion, not just relevance.', 'REMED-EVIDENCE-407-PURPOSE'),
  ('e8cbe31e-4b42-55fb-9bbe-3bfa48876d2f', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20602_davids_harp_projector'), 'B', 'Exclude the evidence for this purpose because Rule 407 bars subsequent remedial measures offered to prove a product defect, design defect, or need for a warning or instruction.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. Gold Key: Rule 407 is not negligence-only. It also bars later remedial measures when offered to prove product defect, design defect, or the need for a warning or instruction. Silver Key: lock the stated purpose first. Naomi is not offering the later hinge and warning to prove a disputed alternative purpose; she is offering them to prove original defect and warning inadequacy. That is the barred purpose lane.', NULL, 'REMED-EVIDENCE-407-PURPOSE'),
  ('db6ffe02-d5e3-5992-b400-499f41494d01', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20602_davids_harp_projector'), 'C', 'Admit the evidence because Rule 407 applies only to negligence claims, not products-liability claims.', 0, '["flat_misstatement","wrong_frame"]', '["negligence_only_rule407","relevance_is_enough","feasibility_magic_word","automatic_exception"]', 'The student remembers the negligence language in Rule 407 and stops there. The breaker is the Gold Key that Rule 407 also covers product defect, design defect, and warning-need uses.', 'The negligence-only version of Rule 407 is too narrow.', 'Recall that Rule 407 includes product defect, design defect, and warning/instruction need.', 'REMED-EVIDENCE-407-PURPOSE'),
  ('f05868ff-2cd9-5a6c-94d3-edcd9bf195b6', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20602_davids_harp_projector'), 'D', 'Admit the evidence automatically because a later redesign always proves feasibility.', 0, '["tiered_absolute","offered_for_purpose"]', '["negligence_only_rule407","relevance_is_enough","feasibility_magic_word","automatic_exception"]', 'Feasibility is a real permitted-purpose word, so the choice feels like it found the exception. The breaker is that feasibility is not automatic and is not the purpose Naomi stated.', 'Feasibility is not automatic; the stem states a barred defect/warning purpose.', 'Match the exception word to the actual purpose stated in the stem.', 'REMED-EVIDENCE-407-PURPOSE'),
  ('46f94bf2-a10a-5e64-af81-3884728f771d', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20603_road_to_emmaus_escape_room'), 'A', 'Yes, because the law should encourage rescue of helpless people.', 0, '["colloquialism"]', '["heroism_equals_liability","rescue_success_required","rescuer_reasonableness_is_dispositive","policy_statement_is_rule"]', 'The student wants to reward rescue as a social good. The breaker is that policy language does not state Daniel''s negligent creation of the peril.', 'The answer gives a policy reason, not the legal test against Daniel''s estate.', 'Cut ''should encourage'' language unless it is tied to the defendant''s legal fault.', 'REM-TORTS-RESCUE-ACTOR-FAULT-01'),
  ('f22882c5-c55b-54d1-85f2-93e5de72f99a', (SELECT question_id FROM questions WHERE external_id = '20603_road_to_emmaus_escape_room'), 'B', 'No, because Daniel''s peril did not arise from his own failure to exercise reasonable care.', 1, '[]', '[]', NULL, 'B is correct. Daniel is the person Ruth sued. The answer must explain why Daniel’s estate is or is not responsible for Ruth’s injury. The stem says Daniel was acting with reasonable care. That fact blocks the rescue-doctrine route against Daniel’s estate.

Gold Key: Rescue doctrine needs a negligent peril-maker. A rescuer’s injury is charged to the person whose negligence created the peril, not merely to the person who needed help.

